0.967—giving a gap of about 18.7 percentage points, which fits within the expected 15-25pp range.\n\nNow I'm thinking through which LLM variants to test on OpenHands. The few-shot-CoT variant performed best on SWE at 0.799, and I'd expect it to reach around 0.76 on OpenHands given the different trajectory structure there, which would put the gap closer to 20 percentage points.\n\nActually, looking at the median tier estimates again—which suggest LLMs perform better on OpenHands than on SWE—I should revise upward. If few-shot-CoT reaches 0.79 or 0.80 on OpenHands, that narrows the gap to around 17-18 percentage points, which fits the expected range. The key insight is that OpenHands trajectories might have clearer stagnation patterns that LLMs can recognize more easily.\n\nNow I'm examining the confidence-1 gold window subset with 282 samples. The gradient boosting and majority vote approaches show similar performance drops here compared to higher-confidence data, with gaps of 1-6 percentage points between them. Looking at the existing high-confidence data (N=505), gradient boosting hits 0.84 while majority vote reaches 0.80, a 4.2 percentage point delta. On the harder confidence-1 subset where labeling functions disagree, I'd expect both methods to perform lower, with gradient boosting around 0.72 and majority vote agreement slightly below that.\n\nThe error decomposition reveals that both methods get it right about 60-65% of the time, both fail on 18-22% of windows, and gradient boosting corrects cases majority vote misses about 8-12% of the time while getting it wrong on 5-8% that majority vote catches. So gradient boosting has a modest edge overall.\n\nFor the cross-agent probe comparison, I'm looking at how well BGE and Qwen transfer from in-domain to zero-shot settings. BGE performs at 0.94 in-domain while Qwen reaches 0.91, but Qwen drops to 0.60 on zero-shot out-of-domain tasks. If BGE transfers at the same ratio, it would land around 0.62 on that same zero-shot task.\n\nLooking at the median tier results, BGE achieves 0.68 zero-shot performance with a 28.7 percentage point gap from the structural baseline of 0.967. E5 performs slightly worse at 0.62 with a 34.7 point gap, suggesting it doesn't transfer as effectively as BGE.\n\nThe coverage analysis shows that the 2-layer fusion configuration only covers about 2.8% of windows from the dataset, which is quite limited.\n\nFor SWE-Agent specifically, the 2-layer fusion coverage jumps to 18.7%, and the command representation fire rate is much higher on SWE compared to OH at only 5.39%, explaining the dramatic coverage gap. With a sample size of 505 and 80% power, I can detect effect sizes around 6-7 percentage points in the median tier.\n\nLooking at the pairwise comparisons, GB versus MV shows a 4.2pp difference with borderline power around 0.65-0.75, while detecting a 6pp difference would give me 80% power. Several of these comparisons are underpowered for smaller effects. On the human ceiling side, the Fleiss kappa is 0.39 with pairwise kappas ranging from 0.33 to 0.485, and the median tier ceiling sits around 0.82-0.87 when looking at raw agreement rates rather than kappa.\n\nNow I'm working through what the actual ceiling should be. Raw agreement is probably around 0.75-0.80, but applying corrections like Spearman-Brown pushes the ceiling estimate up to around 0.84. GB's performance at 0.839 puts it essentially at that ceiling with only a 0.1pp gap, though I'm second-guessing whether that's too tight. If I set the ceiling at 0.845 instead, the gap becomes 0.6pp, which still feels quite small. I need to reconsider what the actual metric range should be here.\n\nLooking at the constraints, human_ceiling_f1 should fall between 0.82 and 0.87, and the gap between GB and ceiling should be 0-3pp. So if ceiling is 0.85 and GB is at 0.839, that gives a 1.1pp gap, which fits within the acceptable range.\n\nFor stride sensitivity, I'm testing stride values of 1, 3, and 5 to see how they affect training set size and bootstrap assumptions. I'd expect stride 1 and 3 to perform similarly, with stride 5 showing a slight performance drop due to having fewer independent windows.\n\nOn the feature importance side, I'm planning a SHAP analysis where I expect the LF-overlap features like command repetition and file diff metrics to dominate, with some residual features showing non-trivial importance as well.\n\nNow I need to think through what I'm actually generating here. The trajectory visualization is just a figure description, not numerical results. I should draft the full YAML output covering all these experiments and their expected outputs. I also need to be careful about which experiments are already completed in the registry versus which ones are still planned—calibration-analysis already has actual results, so I should handle that appropriately rather than generating predictions for something that's already done. I need to focus on just the experiments marked as \"planned\" in the experiment_plan and generate predictions for those, even though calibration-analysis shows completed results in the registry. Let me compile the final YAML with all nine planned experiments.\n\nNow I'm examining the calibration metrics from the registry to see if the actual results align with the predicted tier ranges. The temperature-calibrated ECE of 0.0451 falls right within the median tier prediction of [0.04, 0.06], which validates that prediction. I'll proceed with generating the YAML output with specific numerical predictions for each experiment.\n\nLet me clarify the confidence levels in the gold set—I need to distinguish between the annotator agreement confidence and the labeling function confidence to properly decompose the error analysis. Looking at the actual numbers from the median tier, GB achieves around 0.72 F1 on the conf=1 gold windows while MV agreement sits at roughly 0.70, giving us only about a 2 percentage point delta—which is weaker than expected for the anti-circularity argument and might not even reach statistical significance.\n\nNow I'm ready to write out the full YAML output. For the early termination simulation, I need to work through the specifics: SWE-Agent has roughly 32.6 windows per instance across its dataset, while OH has about 42-44 windows per instance. The stagnation rates differ notably—SWE at 28.46% versus OH at 21.45%—and I'm estimating that around 60% of SWE trajectories and 50% of OH trajectories experience at least one stagnation window, which affects how much compute gets wasted in the tail after stagnation begins.\n\nFor the early termination thresholds, I'm testing different values of k (consecutive stagnation windows): k=3 emerges as the sweet spot, saving about 22% of compute while preserving 91% of task success, which lands nicely in the median efficiency range.\n\nNow I'm comparing the structural detector against baselines on the Pareto curve—it clearly dominates the random approach, though there's still meaningful headroom to the oracle which saves ~40% while preserving 98% success. I need to construct the YAML output with the experiment specifications, including the tier classification, narrative framing, and detailed results tables.\n\nGenerating the YAML structure...\n\nFor the LLM-on-OH experiment, I'm considering which Claude and GPT variants to evaluate and how their performance would differ from SWE-Agent results. The median tier shows stronger LLM performance on OH (0.72-0.82) compared to SWE, likely because stagnation patterns in OH are more semantically interpretable—the command patterns and trajectory characteristics are clearer signals for the judge to work with.\n\nI'm setting my OH baseline estimates with claude_fewshot_cot at 0.78 as the best performer, which gives an 18.7 percentage point gap to the structural GB baseline of 0.967—right in the expected 15-25pp range.\n\nNow I'm moving into the cross-agent-probe-bge analysis, looking at BGE-M3's in-domain performance on SWE with notable variance across seeds, and starting to examine Qwen's results.\n\nQwen's zero-shot transfer to OH drops significantly to 0.598, well below its in-domain 0.9055, while BGE performs better at 0.68 median tier—likely due to its multilingual training and larger model capacity helping it capture more diverse stagnation patterns. E5 shows similar transfer challenges with a 0.63 zero-shot result on OH, creating even larger gaps from the structural baseline.\n\nThe encoder experiments reveal that while BGE narrows the performance gap from Qwen's 36.9pp down to 28.7pp, semantic embeddings fundamentally struggle with cross-agent transfer compared to structural features, which suggests the advantage is encoder-robust rather than encoder-independent.\n\nNow I'm looking at the 2-LF coverage across agents—SWE-Agent has about 18.7% of windows meeting the confidence threshold, while OH's coverage appears much lower at roughly 2.8% based on the window counts. wait, let me think about what \"2-LF coverage\" means on OH more carefully.\n\nWith only cmd_rep + file_diff (no OB):\n- A window gets conf≥2 only if both LFs agree\n- On OH, cmd_rep only fires on 5.39% of windows → most windows only have file_diff's opinion\n- So conf≥2 requires cmd_rep to fire AND agree with file_diff\n\nOH 2-LF conf≥2: 4017/143057 = 2.8%\nOH 2-LF conf≥1: 72554/143057 = 50.7%\n\nFor SWE-Agent:\n2-LF conf≥2: 10243/54809 = 18.7%\n\nThis deployment coverage gap is stark—only 2.8% of OH windows would get confident predictions with the 2-LF setup, which severely limits early termination's practical utility. SWE-Agent fares better at 18.7%, and stagnation windows might have higher coverage since they typically involve command repetition that triggers cmd_rep.\n\nLooking at the SHAP analysis on the GB model with 30 structural features, I expect the top contributors to be cmd_rep count, file_diff score, unique_commands ratio, and output similarity—features that overlap heavily with the LF inputs and reinforce the circularity concern. However, some non-LF features like trajectory position, step count variance, and error count do show meaningful importance, with roughly 70% of total SHAP value coming from LF-correlated features.\n\nFor the trajectory visualization, I'll show a few representative cases: one where all LFs agree on stagnation, one where they disagree, and one false positive case, overlaying the LF activations to illustrate how structural features evolve. Then for stride sensitivity, I'm testing stride 1 (current baseline with all overlapping windows), stride 3 (about a third of windows with more independence), and stride 5 (a fifth of windows, most independent), expecting performance to stay robust around 0.895–0.905 for stride 3 and drop slightly to 0.87–0.89 for stride 5, which would validate that overlapping windows aren't driving the results.\n\nIn the median tier, stride 3 shows a 2–3 percentage point drop and stride 5 drops 5–7 points, so while the bootstrap independence assumption is partially violated at stride 1, stride 3 is close enough that the core findings still hold. Now I'm ready to write out the full YAML configuration, and I should note that several of these experiments will produce tables and figures—early termination metrics, compute waste summaries, Pareto operating points, LLM-on-OH results, confusion matrices for gold decomposition, cross-agent probe results, coverage rates, and power analysis tables.\n\nI'm also mapping out the figures: Pareto curves, calibration reliability diagrams, SHAP plots, trajectory visualizations, and power curves. One thing I need to clarify is that calibration-analysis is marked as \"planned\" in the experiment plan but already completed in the registry, and since the actual ECE result of 0.0451 falls within the median range, I should include it with the real results rather than treating it as pending.\n\nNow I'm constructing the YAML output carefully. For the LLM-on-OpenHands experiment, I need to be precise about what makes it valuable: it's a matched comparison where both structural and LLM approaches evaluate the same OpenHands trajectories, which addresses the apples-to-oranges problem from the previous SWE-Agent comparison. The main constraint is computational cost—evaluating all 143K windows with LLM judgment would be prohibitively expensive, so I need to determine a reasonable sample size.\n\nLooking at the cost structure from the SWE baseline, a subsample of around 2000-3000 windows seems practical. For the narrative framing in the median tier, I'm shifting the language from \"dominance\" to \"substantial practical advantage,\" describing the structural cross-agent transfer of 0.967 as \"strong\" rather than \"near-perfect,\" and characterizing the LLM performance gap of 15-25 percentage points as \"substantial.\"\n\nFor the probe gap and early termination findings, I'm being more measured—the gap persists across encoders though the magnitude varies, and early termination offers moderate compute savings with an acceptable trade-off in task success. The gold set evidence is suggestive rather than conclusive, and I need to include an honest limitations section.\n\nNow examining the compute-waste-audit specifics: the SWE-Agent trajectories span roughly 1683 instances with an average of 32.6 windows per instance and a 28.46% stagnation rate. For the stagnation tail analysis, I'm identifying the first stagnation window in each trajectory and counting the remaining steps, noting that some trajectories recover after stagnation. The data suggests around 55% of SWE trajectories contain at least one stagnation window, compared to roughly 45% for OH trajectories.\n\nLooking at the stagnating trajectories themselves, the median tail runs about 8-12 windows out of the ~33 average, representing roughly 25-35% of the total trajectory length. But when I account for all trajectories including non-stagnating ones, that gives me only 16.5% waste, which is too low for the 25-40% range I'm seeing. I think I need to reframe this—compute waste likely refers to failed trajectories specifically, where the agent spent compute after stagnation began. Since resolved trajectories have nearly immunity with a 1.3% error rate, stagnation concentrates in unresolved cases, and SWE-Agent only resolves about 23% of trajectories.\n\nFor unresolved trajectories, stagnation typically kicks in around 40-60% through the trajectory, meaning that proportion of compute is wasted post-stagnation. So overall waste is roughly 77% unresolved times 42% post-stagnation compute, giving me about 32%—right in that 25-40% range. I'll use 32% as my median estimate, with OH probably around 28% given its lower stagnation rate of 21.45%.\n\nNow for the early termination simulation, I need to think through what different k values would do. Starting with k=1 means terminating after just one stagnation window, but that risks too many false positives from transient stagnation.\n\nLooking at the tradeoffs across k values: k=1 saves the most compute at around 40% but tanks task success to 78%, k=2 is more conservative at 30% savings with 86% success, k=3 hits a good balance point saving 24% while preserving 91% success, and k=5 is very conservative at only 15% savings but maintains 96% success. The oracle detector would save 42% while preserving 99%, whereas a random baseline with the same 24% savings rate as k=3 only preserves 76% success—showing clear Pareto advantage for the structural detector.\n\nI think I have the detail I need now to write out the YAML.\n\nNow I'm thinking through how to structure the analysis field for each experiment to connect the results back to the paper's narrative and claims. I need to be precise about what goes into the YAML format—tables should be specifications or descriptions rather than actual table data, and figures_description should explain what visualizations would show. Let me organize the planned experiments systematically and make sure I'm covering everything comprehensively before I write the full YAML block. From experiment_plan, status: planned:\n1. early-termination-simulation (C4, P0)\n2. compute-waste-audit (C4, P0)\n3. cost-effectiveness-pareto (C4, P0, depends on 1+2)\n4. llm-on-oh (C1, P0)\n5. conf1-gold-error-decomposition (C1, P0, depends on gold-set which is DONE)\n6. cross-agent-probe-bge (C1, P0)\n7. cross-agent-probe-e5 (C1, P0)\n8. 2lf-coverage-analysis (C4, P0)\n9. calibration-analysis (C1, P0) — already DONE in registry\n10. gold-power-analysis (all, P1)\n11. human-ceiling-estimate (all, P1)\n12. stride-sensitivity (C1, P1)\n13. feature-importance-figure (C1, P1)\n14. trajectory-visualization (all, P1)\n\nThat's 14 experiments total. The user wants detailed data predictions for each planned experiment, so I'll generate those across all of them. For calibration-analysis since it's already complete, I'll use the actual results rather than predictions. I'm skipping the three experiments in \"PREPARING\" status since they're not in the planned list.\n\nNow I need to write out the YAML with specific predicted metrics for each experiment. Let me think through reasonable numbers for early-termination-simulation first — I'll predict precision, recall, compute savings, and task success preservation across different k thresholds for both SWE-Agent and OpenHands.\n\nFor SWE-Agent, as k increases, precision goes up but recall drops off, which makes sense since we're being more conservative about early stopping. The compute savings decrease as we stop less frequently. For OpenHands, I'm seeing similar patterns with slightly different magnitudes.\n\nThe sweet spot appears to be around k=3 for SWE-Agent where we save 23% compute while preserving 91% of task success, and k=2-3 for OpenHands with comparable tradeoffs.\n\nNow moving into the compute-waste-audit section where I'll detail the breakdown of wasted computation across different trajectory types. Now I'm looking at performance metrics on a stratified sample of 2000 windows, where Claude's various approaches range from 0.71 to 0.78, but the structural gradient boosting model achieves 0.965—a substantial 18.5 percentage point gap. For the confidence-1 gold standard windows, the gradient boosting model shows an F1 of 0.72 with 62% agreement on correct predictions, though it only edges out majority voting by about 2.5 percentage points overall when accounting for cases where each method gets it right or wrong.\n\nThe bootstrap p-value of 0.032 suggests this difference is statistically significant. When I look at cross-agent probing with BGE and E5 embeddings, both show much lower performance—BGE reaches 0.72 on high-confidence windows while E5 only gets to 0.66—leaving gaps of 27-34 percentage points compared to the structural model. Finally, examining coverage across the SWE-Agent dataset, about 28% of the 54,809 total windows have at least 3 labeling functions with confidence ≥2, and another 19% have exactly 2 such functions.\n\nFor OpenHands, the situation is quite different: while 30% of windows have 3+ high-confidence labeling functions, only 2.8% have 2 high-confidence ones, creating a dramatic coverage gap that stems from the low command repetition fire rate of just 5.39%. The calibration analysis is complete and shows the model's expected calibration error improves from 0.0606 to 0.0451 after temperature calibration, landing within the target range.\n\nFor the power analysis with 505 samples, I can detect effects of 6 percentage points or larger at standard significance levels, but the observed 4.2pp difference between models falls short of this threshold—I'd need around 8-10 percentage points to achieve reasonable power. Finally, I'm estimating the human ceiling by treating each pair of annotators as a model-versus-gold comparison and averaging their individual F1 scores against the consensus of the other two annotators. Looking at the individual F1 scores against the majority label, I'm getting values around 0.83-0.87 with a mean of 0.85, which puts the GB score of 0.839 just below the ceiling. But I need to reconsider how to properly calculate this—using a leave-one-out approach where each annotator is evaluated against the majority of the other two would be more rigorous, since including an annotator in their own gold standard inflates their agreement artificially.\n\nWith three annotators, the majority of the other two only exists when they agree, which happens at different rates depending on the pair. Looking at the pairwise kappas, B2 and B3 agree about 70% of the time, while the other pairs agree around 73-76% of the time. This means for each annotator, I'd have roughly 350+ windows where I can compute a proper ceiling against the other two's agreement.\n\nNow I'm working through the actual F1 scores against leave-one-out majorities. The individual ceilings come out to around 0.82-0.86, averaging about 0.84 or 0.85. The model's at 0.839, so the gap is minimal—basically 1 percentage point. But I need to think about what this ceiling really means given that the annotators themselves only reach κ=0.39 overall. The gold standard itself has inherent noise from disagreement, so there's a fundamental limit to how well any model can perform.\n\nFor the median tier report, I'll use 0.85 as the ceiling estimate and note that the model's 0.839 sits comfortably within about 1.1 percentage points of that. Now looking at stride sensitivity—when I increase the stride from 1 to 3 to 5, performance drops from 0.906 to 0.895 to 0.878, but the training set shrinks dramatically from 38k windows down to 7.6k. The performance degradation tracks with the data reduction rather than the stride parameter itself.\n\nFor confidence intervals, stride=1 likely gives anticonservative bounds since overlapping windows violate independence assumptions, while stride=3 offers better calibration and stride=5 produces the widest, most honest intervals.\n\nLooking at feature importance through SHAP values, the top drivers are command repetition count, file diff score, and unique commands ratio, with the remaining features showing diminishing contributions. About 65% of the important features correlate with the labeling function, which suggests the model is picking up on meaningful signal.\n\nNow I'm planning the trajectory visualizations with three representative cases: one showing clear stagnation where all labeling functions agree, another with ambiguous behavior where they disagree, and a false positive where the agent appears stuck but is actually making progress. Each will have a timeline showing step progression, labeling function activations as colored bars, model confidence as a line, and the ground truth label when available.\n\nI'm also reconsidering the cost estimates for the LLM-on-OH experiment—evaluating around 2000 windows would run roughly $12.78 for zero-shot prompting and significantly more for few-shot, so that's a meaningful constraint to keep in mind.\n\nThe key insight is that I need to evaluate both the structural baseline and the LLM on the exact same subset of windows for a fair comparison, since the structural model is already benchmarked across all 143K windows. Using N=2000 windows would match the scale of the SWE evaluation and keep costs reasonable.\n\nNow I'm clarifying what the confidence metric means in the gold set—it's the LF confidence score, indicating how many labeling functions agree on a label. The 282 windows with conf=1 from the 505-window gold set B are cases where only one LF fires for a label while others abstain or disagree, representing the harder, more uncertain cases.\n\nOn windows where LFs agree (conf≥2), the silver labels are reliable so the model should match them well. But on the 282 conf=1 windows where LFs disagree, this is where I can really test whether GB has learned meaningful patterns—majority vote would just follow the single firing LF and achieve around 70% accuracy, while GB with its learned soft boundaries reaches about 72%, suggesting it's capturing something beyond simple LF voting.\n\nBreaking down the error patterns: among these 282 windows, majority vote gets 197 correct and 85 wrong, while GB improves to 203 correct with 79 wrong. The key insight is how many errors GB fixes that MV gets wrong versus where they both fail or both succeed. Let me verify the math checks out, then recalculate using McNemar's test—I get p=0.22, which isn't significant. I think the issue is I should be working with F1 scores rather than raw accuracy, since that's what the paper reports, so let me reconsider the baseline numbers.\n\nLooking at the median tier estimates, I see GB F1 around 0.72 and MV agreement around 0.71, but these are measuring different things—MV agreement is essentially an accuracy metric while GB F1 is a macro F1 score. They're not directly comparable, so I need to find a better way to compute the actual difference.\n\nNow I'm examining the performance breakdown across the 282 samples. GB achieves 75% accuracy compared to MV's 71%, with both methods getting about 67% of cases right. The key insight is that GB outperforms MV on 22 cases while MV only beats GB on 10 cases. Running McNemar's test on this difference gives me a chi-squared value of 4.5 with p ≈ 0.034, which puts it right at the borderline of statistical significance.\n\nI'm ready to compile the results now. Let me verify the structural versus LLM gap is consistent with my numbers—if structural GB achieves 0.967 on the overall set and the best LLM reaches 0.78, that's an 18.7pp gap, which fits the expected 15-25pp range. Even accounting for slight variation on subsamples, this checks out.\n\nFor the cross-agent probe experiments, I'm seeing BGE zero-shot at 0.685 as the strongest performer, which gives a 28.2pp gap against structural GB—solidly in the 20-37pp range and confirming the \"encoder-robust\" framing rather than \"encoder-independent.\" The existing Qwen result at 0.598 was wider at 36.9pp, so BGE represents a meaningful improvement while still maintaining that robustness gap.\n\nNow I'm looking at the cost-effectiveness Pareto curve for the structural detector, which plots compute saved against task success preserved across different k values, showing how the tradeoff evolves from k=1 through k=5.\n\nThe curve sits between the oracle performance and random baseline, revealing that while the structural approach beats random, the gains plateau quickly—you can't achieve more than 30% compute savings without sacrificing below 90% task success. For SWE-bench specifically, since the baseline resolution rate is around 23%, most trajectories fail anyway, so stagnation-based early termination that correctly identifies doomed trajectories doesn't actually lose task success because those tasks were going to fail regardless.\n\nThe real risk is false positives—incorrectly flagging a trajectory as stagnant when it's actually recovering—which could kill a successful run. But with the error analysis showing only 1.3% false positive rate on resolved trajectories, requiring three consecutive false positives to trigger termination makes wrongly killing a successful trajectory quite rare, resulting in roughly a 2% absolute drop in task success preservation.\n\nSo I'm looking at the tradeoff: 23% compute savings for a 2.1% absolute hit in resolution rate, which seems reasonable. For the Pareto analysis, I should show both the relative metric (task success preserved percentage) and the practical impact (absolute resolution rate change).\n\nNow I'm computing the 2-LF coverage on SWE-Agent using the data I have—10243 out of 15401 windows with confidence ≥2, giving 66.5% coverage—and checking how this scales across the full dataset.\n\nLooking at the coverage metrics across both datasets: SWE has 10243 2-LF windows with confidence ≥2 out of 54809 total (18.7% coverage), while OH shows 4017 2-LF windows with confidence ≥2 compared to 43376 3-LF windows with confidence ≥2, which is only 9.3% coverage.\n\nThe 2-LF configuration's -1.8pp performance degradation is measured on this small 9.3% subset of OH windows, leaving 90.7% without confident predictions. However, if I look at confidence ≥1 for 2-LF (where at least one LF fires), the coverage jumps to 72554 out of 143057 windows, or about 50.7% of OH windows.\n\nFor deployment, I'm weighing three options: using lower-confidence predictions at conf≥1, defaulting uncertain windows to \"progress,\" or relying on structural features that work across all windows regardless of LF coverage. This actually makes a strong case for structural features since they don't depend on labeling function availability.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the Pareto efficiency metric for the experiment—calculating the area under the Pareto frontier normalized against oracle and random baselines to see how well the structural detector trades off between coverage and accuracy.\n\nThe structural detector captures about 67% of the theoretically achievable improvement over random, which is solid. Now I'm moving forward with writing the YAML configuration.\n\nFor stride sensitivity, I'm also considering how the bootstrap confidence intervals widen with larger strides—stride=1 gives tighter CIs around ±0.008 for macro F1, but stride=5 widens to ±0.018, reflecting the reduced effective sample size but providing more honest independence estimates.\n\nLooking at feature importance, the key insight is that while labeling-function-correlated features dominate, about 30% of importance comes from non-LF features, which explains why gradient boosting can outperform majority voting by learning additional structural signals beyond what the labeling functions directly capture.\n\nNow examining variance metrics like count variance, error count, and command diversity entropy to round out the analysis.\n\nFor the narrative guidance at the median tier, I need to dial back the claims from \"dominance\" to \"substantial practical advantage,\" reframe the headline around strong cross-agent transfer with zero target-domain data, and adjust the confidence level from conclusive to suggestive evidence. Where encoder probe gaps fall below 25 percentage points, I should remove \"encoder-independent\" language and instead note that the gap persists across encoders though the magnitude varies. The early termination claim should shift to describing moderate compute savings with acceptable task success trade-offs.\n\nWriting the YAML response now...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":46795,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":46795},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b59b9a83-69fa-419b-a48e-3103bddb8d61","uuid":"0ba5265b-b992-46d7-959a-94bd89fc6754"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BLXjswDxuNbvJiB5NSCcFY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Claims 需全面调低强度。Headline 从 \"dominance\" 降为 \"substantial practical advantage\"：\n  \"Structural features achieve strong cross-agent transfer (0.967) with zero target-domain data,\n  outperforming best LLM judge by ~19pp and zero-shot neural probes by 20-37pp depending on encoder.\"\n  conf=1 gold 证据定性为 suggestive（\"GB shows improved performance on LF-disagreement windows,\n  though the gold set is underpowered for fine-grained stratified analysis\"）。\n  BGE probe zero-shot 缩小 gap 至 ~28pp，去掉 \"encoder-independent\"，改为 \"gap persists\n  across encoders though magnitude varies (28-37pp)\"。Claim 4 early termination 改为\n  \"moderate compute savings with acceptable task success trade-off\"——best operating point\n  saves ~23% compute while preserving ~91% task success，Pareto 曲线存在但不陡峭。\n  新增 honest limitations 段：(1) N=505 gold 只能检测 ≥6pp effect，observed 4.2pp delta underpowered；\n  (2) human ceiling ~0.85，GB 0.839 close but interpretation ambiguous；(3) 2-LF deployable config\n  在 OH 上 conf≥2 覆盖率仅 9.3%，实际部署需 fallback strategy。\n  TLM negative (C3) 和 label quality bottleneck (C2) 不受影响，作为稳定分析贡献。\n  R2 novelty 通过 methodology 贡献（anti-circularity 框架 + 2-LF deployable design）部分缓解，\n  但 reviewer 可能仍要求更多 non-SE agent 验证。Projected consensus 3.5-4/6。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"Early Termination Simulation\"\n    plan_id: \"early-termination-simulation\"\n    description: \"在 SWE-Agent 和 OH 全量轨迹上模拟不同 consecutive-stagnation threshold k 的 early stopping policy，量化 precision/recall/compute savings/task success trade-off\"\n    expected_results:\n      swe_agent:\n        n_trajectories: 1683\n        n_trajectories_with_stagnation: 1044\n        k1:\n          precision_stag: 0.81\n          recall_stag: 0.94\n          compute_saved_pct: 38.2\n          task_success_preserved_pct: 78.4\n          n_terminated: 987\n          n_false_kills: 41\n        k2:\n          precision_stag: 0.87\n          recall_stag: 0.85\n          compute_saved_pct: 28.7\n          task_success_preserved_pct: 86.3\n          n_terminated: 831\n          n_false_kills: 22\n        k3:\n          precision_stag: 0.91\n          recall_stag: 0.76\n          compute_saved_pct: 22.8\n          task_success_preserved_pct: 91.2\n          n_terminated: 694\n          n_false_kills: 12\n        k5:\n          precision_stag: 0.95\n          recall_stag: 0.58\n          compute_saved_pct: 14.1\n          task_success_preserved_pct: 96.1\n          n_terminated: 482\n          n_false_kills: 4\n        k7:\n          precision_stag: 0.97\n          recall_stag: 0.42\n          compute_saved_pct: 8.6\n          task_success_preserved_pct: 98.3\n          n_terminated: 328\n          n_false_kills: 1\n        best_operating_point: k3\n      openhands:\n        n_trajectories: 3409\n        k1:\n          compute_saved_pct: 33.1\n          task_success_preserved_pct: 80.2\n        k2:\n          compute_saved_pct: 24.6\n          task_success_preserved_pct: 87.8\n        k3:\n          compute_saved_pct: 18.9\n          task_success_preserved_pct: 92.4\n        k5:\n          compute_saved_pct: 10.7\n          task_success_preserved_pct: 96.8\n        best_operating_point: k3\n      oracle_swe_k3:\n        compute_saved_pct: 38.5\n        task_success_preserved_pct: 99.2\n      random_baseline_swe_at_23pct_savings:\n        task_success_preserved_pct: 76.4\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 early termination 效果 moderate：k=3 作为最佳 operating point 节省 ~23% 计算\n      但 task success 降至 ~91%。原因：(1) GB structural detector 在 silver labels 上 F1=0.967\n      但 gold 验证 F1=0.839，real-world precision 不如 silver eval 显示的高；(2) 连续 3 窗口\n      false positive 概率虽低，但在 ~1683 条轨迹中仍累积出 ~12 条 false kills；(3) OH 上\n      stagnation rate 更低 (21.45% vs 28.46%)，可回收的 compute 本身更少，所以 savings 比 SWE\n      低约 4pp；(4) 与 oracle 对比显示 structural detector 只达到理论最优的 ~59%（22.8/38.5），\n      因为 detector 延迟识别 stagnation onset（median lag ~2-3 windows）且有 FP 导致误杀。\n      Pareto 曲线存在但斜率不够陡——想获得 >30% savings 必须接受 task success 降到 <87%。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Early Termination Operating Points\"\n        columns: [\"k\", \"Precision\", \"Recall\", \"Compute Saved (%)\", \"Task Success Preserved (%)\", \"N Terminated\", \"N False Kills\"]\n        description: \"SWE-Agent 上不同 threshold k 的完整 trade-off 矩阵，附 OH 对应行\"\n      - name: \"Table: Agent-Specific Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Agent\", \"Best k\", \"Savings (%)\", \"Success Preserved (%)\", \"Resolution Rate Impact\"]\n        description: \"SWE-Agent vs OH 最佳 operating point 对比\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Precision-Recall curve for early termination across k values, with iso-savings contours\"\n    analysis: >\n      k=3 是 SWE-Agent 上的最佳 operating point（23% savings, 91% preserved），OH 上 k=3\n      也接近最优（19% savings, 92% preserved）。Savings 差异源于 OH stagnation rate 更低。\n      实际部署价值：SWE-Agent 23% savings 对应约 $2.3/100 trajectories 的 API cost 节省\n      （假设 average $10/trajectory）。但 9% task success 损失意味着 resolution rate 从\n      ~23% 降至 ~21%——对于 SWE-bench 这样的 benchmark 影响可观。论文需要诚实呈现\n      \"moderate savings with non-trivial trade-off\" 而非 \"compute-efficient\"。\n\n  - name: \"Compute Waste Audit\"\n    plan_id: \"compute-waste-audit\"\n    description: \"回溯分析全量轨迹的 stagnation tail——从首次真正停滞到轨迹结束的 wasted steps/tokens/time\"\n    expected_results:\n      swe_agent:\n        n_trajectories: 1683\n        trajectories_with_any_stagnation_pct: 61.8\n        trajectories_with_sustained_stagnation_pct: 48.3\n        median_stagnation_onset_position: 0.43\n        mean_stagnation_onset_position: 0.47\n        median_tail_length_windows: 9\n        mean_tail_length_windows: 12.7\n        compute_waste_steps_pct: 34.2\n        compute_waste_tokens_pct: 31.8\n        compute_waste_time_pct: 33.5\n        wasted_steps_total: 142500\n        wasted_tokens_total_millions: 15.3\n        by_resolution:\n          resolved_waste_pct: 8.2\n          unresolved_waste_pct: 41.7\n      openhands:\n        n_trajectories: 3409\n        trajectories_with_any_stagnation_pct: 52.4\n        compute_waste_steps_pct: 27.6\n        compute_waste_tokens_pct: 25.1\n        median_tail_length_windows: 7\n      combined:\n        compute_waste_steps_pct: 31.4\n        compute_waste_tokens_pct: 28.9\n      tail_length_distribution:\n        p25_windows: 4\n        p50_windows: 8\n        p75_windows: 16\n        p90_windows: 28\n        max_windows: 89\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 compute waste 在 25-40% 范围内，取 ~32%。推理：(1) SWE-Agent stagnation rate\n      28.46%，但 stagnation 集中在轨迹后半段（error analysis 显示 late_66_100 区间占 59% 的\n      test windows），所以 onset 位置 median ~0.43 意味着 tail 长度约占总轨迹 57%；(2) 但并非\n      所有 stagnation 后的 steps 都是 waste——agent 可能有短暂恢复再次停滞，实际 \"pure waste\"\n      低于 raw tail 长度；(3) resolved 轨迹 waste 极低（8.2%），因为成功轨迹中短暂 stagnation\n      后恢复是常态（error analysis: resolved 仅 1.3% error rate）；(4) unresolved 轨迹贡献\n      绝大部分 waste（41.7%），且这些轨迹占 ~77% 的总量——所以 overall waste = 77%×41.7%\n      + 23%×8.2% ≈ 34%；(5) OH waste 更低因为 stagnation rate 更低且轨迹更长（更多\n      productive steps 稀释 waste ratio）。Token waste 略低于 step waste 因为 stagnation\n      windows 的 token count 通常低于 progress windows（重复命令更短）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Compute Waste Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Agent\", \"Traj with Stag (%)\", \"Onset Position (median)\", \"Tail Length (median)\", \"Waste Steps (%)\", \"Waste Tokens (%)\"]\n        description: \"SWE-Agent 和 OH 的 compute waste 摘要\"\n      - name: \"Table: Waste by Resolution Status\"\n        columns: [\"Status\", \"N Trajectories\", \"Waste Steps (%)\", \"Contribution to Total Waste (%)\"]\n        description: \"按任务解决状态分层的 waste 分析\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Histogram of stagnation tail lengths (windows), with vertical lines at p50 and p90\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: trajectory length vs waste ratio, colored by resolution status\"\n    analysis: >\n      ~32% compute waste 支撑 Claim 4 的 motivation，但数字本身需要 caveat：(1) waste 定义\n      依赖 stagnation label 质量——gold validation 显示 GB F1=0.839，非 perfect，所以 waste\n      边界有 ±5pp 不确定性；(2) unresolved 轨迹贡献 92% 的 total waste，resolved 轨迹几乎\n      没有 waste——说明 early termination 主要在 \"注定失败\" 的轨迹上节省计算；(3) tail 长度\n      分布高度右偏（p90=28 vs p50=8），少数极长 stagnation tail 拉高均值。\n      论文表述：报告 median 和 IQR 而非 mean，避免被极端值误导。\n\n  - name: \"Cost-Effectiveness Pareto Curve\"\n    plan_id: \"cost-effectiveness-pareto\"\n    description: \"Pareto 前沿：横轴 compute saved (%)，纵轴 task success preserved (%)，structural vs oracle vs random\"\n    expected_results:\n      structural_pareto_points:\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 8.6, task_success_pct: 98.3, k: 7}\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 14.1, task_success_pct: 96.1, k: 5}\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 22.8, task_success_pct: 91.2, k: 3}\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 28.7, task_success_pct: 86.3, k: 2}\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 38.2, task_success_pct: 78.4, k: 1}\n      oracle_pareto_points:\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 15.0, task_success_pct: 99.5}\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 25.0, task_success_pct: 99.0}\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 38.5, task_success_pct: 98.6}\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 42.0, task_success_pct: 97.1}\n      random_baseline_points:\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 10.0, task_success_pct: 89.8}\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 20.0, task_success_pct: 79.6}\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 30.0, task_success_pct: 69.5}\n      structural_aupf: 0.847\n      oracle_aupf: 0.952\n      random_aupf: 0.643\n      structural_efficiency_ratio: 0.66\n      structural_dominates_random: true\n      gap_to_oracle_significant: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Pareto 曲线存在但斜率 moderate：structural detector 明确优于 random（AUPF 0.847 vs 0.643），\n      但与 oracle 有显著 gap（0.952）。Efficiency ratio 0.66 意味着 structural detector 只\n      实现了理论最优改进的 66%。原因：(1) detector 延迟 ~2-3 windows 才识别 stagnation onset，\n      这些 lag windows 不可回收；(2) false positive 在 k=1-2 时显著——error analysis 显示 FP\n      dominant（65%）且 highly confident（mean prob=0.922），low-k termination 会 kill\n      recovering trajectories；(3) false negative 累积效应——一些长期 stagnation 轨迹从未\n      触发连续 k 个检测（recall 随 k 增大下降快），无法 terminate。Oracle 的优势在于\n      perfect onset detection + zero FP，消除了 lag 和 误杀。Random baseline 线性下降\n      因为随机终止等概率 kill 任意轨迹，与 stagnation 状态无关。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Pareto Operating Points\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"k/threshold\", \"Compute Saved (%)\", \"Task Success (%)\", \"Resolution Rate\"]\n        description: \"Structural / Oracle / Random 的 Pareto 前沿对比\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Pareto curve: X=compute saved (%), Y=task success preserved (%). Three curves: structural (blue, solid), oracle (green, dashed), random (red, dotted). Shaded area between structural and random = efficiency gain.\"\n      - \"Bar chart: structural efficiency ratio at different operating points\"\n    analysis: >\n      Pareto 分析支撑 \"detection-to-intervention\" 叙事但需降调：从 \"compute-efficient early\n      termination\" 改为 \"moderate compute savings with acceptable task success trade-off\"。\n      Efficiency ratio 0.66 说明 structural detector 远非 oracle，改进空间大——future work\n      可通过更好的 stagnation onset 检测（减少 lag）和 calibrated confidence（减少 FP）\n      来逼近 oracle。论文最佳呈现方式：Pareto 图作为 main figure，配 3 条曲线和 shaded\n      efficiency region，让 reviewer 自行判断 \"moderate savings\" 是否有价值。\n\n  - name: \"LLM-on-OH Matched Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"llm-on-oh\"\n    description: \"在 OpenHands 轨迹上评估 LLM-as-judge（多种 prompting），与 structural GB 在相同数据上直接对比\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_set:\n        n_windows: 2000\n        sampling: stratified by confidence and stagnation label\n        oh_subset: true\n      claude_zeroshot:\n        macro_f1: 0.706\n        f1_stag: 0.641\n        f1_prog: 0.771\n        cost_usd: 12.8\n        parse_failures: 3\n      claude_fewshot:\n        macro_f1: 0.762\n        f1_stag: 0.703\n        f1_prog: 0.821\n        cost_usd: 39.2\n        parse_failures: 0\n      claude_cot:\n        macro_f1: 0.738\n        f1_stag: 0.678\n        f1_prog: 0.798\n        cost_usd: 18.9\n        parse_failures: 5\n      claude_fewshot_cot:\n        macro_f1: 0.781\n        f1_stag: 0.724\n        f1_prog: 0.838\n        cost_usd: 44.1\n        parse_failures: 1\n        note: best LLM variant\n      structural_gb_on_same_subset:\n        macro_f1: 0.965\n        f1_stag: 0.946\n        f1_prog: 0.984\n      gap_best_llm_vs_structural_pp: 18.4\n      best_llm_variant: claude_fewshot_cot\n      swe_vs_oh_llm_comparison:\n        swe_best_llm_f1: 0.799\n        oh_best_llm_f1: 0.781\n        delta_pp: -1.8\n      bootstrap_structural_vs_best_llm:\n        delta: 0.184\n        ci_95: [0.162, 0.206]\n        p: 0.0001\n      total_cost_usd: 115.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLM 在 OH 上 F1 ~0.78（best variant），比 SWE 上略低 1.8pp。原因：(1) OH 轨迹\n      结构与 SWE-Agent 不同——OH 使用 browsing/coding 混合操作，stagnation 形态更多样化，\n      LLM 的 few-shot exemplars（来自 SWE-Agent 模式）迁移能力有限；(2) OH stagnation rate\n      更低 (21.45%)，class imbalance 更严重，LLM 倾向于 predict progress on ambiguous windows；\n      (3) 但 OH 的 stagnation 形态在语义上可能更 \"明显\"——OH agent 停滞时经常表现为\n      browsing 同一网页 or 重复相同的 coding pattern，LLM 能识别这些模式（所以 F1 没有\n      大幅下降）；(4) structural GB 在 OH 上保持 0.965（与整体 0.967 一致），因为 structural\n      features 不依赖语义理解。Gap 18.4pp 仍然显著（p<0.001），但从 SWE 的 16.8pp 并无\n      明显变化——structural 和 LLM 的相对优势在跨 agent 时稳定。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: LLM-on-OH Results\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Macro F1\", \"F1 Stag\", \"F1 Prog\", \"Cost ($)\", \"Parse Failures\"]\n        description: \"OH 上所有 LLM 变体 + structural GB 的完整对比\"\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-Agent LLM Consistency\"\n        columns: [\"LLM Variant\", \"SWE F1\", \"OH F1\", \"Delta (pp)\"]\n        description: \"同一 LLM variant 在 SWE vs OH 上的性能对比\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: SWE vs OH performance for each LLM variant + structural GB, with error bars from bootstrap CI\"\n    analysis: >\n      LLM-on-OH 结果消除了 \"evaluation scope mismatch\" concern：structural 和 LLM 在相同\n      OH 数据上直接对比，gap 18.4pp 是 clean matched comparison。Headline 可以写\n      \"structural features outperform best LLM judge by ~18pp on matched cross-agent evaluation\"。\n      但 18.4pp 应表述为 \"substantial\" 而非 \"overwhelming\"，因为 LLM 0.78 本身不算差\n      （远超 random 0.50），且 LLM 不需要任何训练数据。论文需承认 LLM 的优势：zero-setup、\n      interpretable judgment、可以给出 reasoning。Structural 的优势：speed (<5ms vs seconds)、\n      cost ($0 vs $44/2000 windows)、accuracy (+18pp)。\n\n  - name: \"Conf=1 Gold Error Decomposition\"\n    plan_id: \"conf1-gold-error-decomposition\"\n    description: \"在 282 个 conf=1 gold 窗口（LFs 分歧）上分解 GB-correct-MV-wrong vs GB-wrong-MV-correct vs both-correct vs both-wrong\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_conf1_gold: 282\n      gold_label_distribution:\n        stagnation: 118\n        progress: 164\n      gb_on_conf1:\n        macro_f1: 0.718\n        accuracy: 0.745\n        f1_stag: 0.672\n        f1_prog: 0.764\n        n_correct: 210\n      mv_on_conf1:\n        agreement_with_gold: 0.709\n        n_correct: 200\n      decomposition:\n        both_correct: 186\n        both_correct_pct: 65.96\n        gb_correct_mv_wrong: 24\n        gb_correct_mv_wrong_pct: 8.51\n        gb_wrong_mv_correct: 14\n        gb_wrong_mv_correct_pct: 4.96\n        both_wrong: 58\n        both_wrong_pct: 20.57\n      net_gb_advantage_windows: 10\n      net_gb_advantage_pp: 3.55\n      mcnemar_chi2: 2.63\n      mcnemar_p: 0.035\n      bootstrap_delta_f1:\n        delta: 0.032\n        ci_95: [0.003, 0.068]\n        p: 0.028\n      gb_corrects_mv_pattern: \"GB 正确修正的 24 个窗口中，68% 涉及 file_diff 与 cmd_rep 的分歧，GB 学到了 file_diff 在 transition 区域更可靠的软规则\"\n      gb_fails_mv_correct_pattern: \"GB 错误的 14 个窗口中，79% 是 OB 信号与其他 LFs 冲突，GB 过度依赖 OB 的 lagging 信号\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 conf=1 gold 证据是 suggestive 而非 conclusive。原因：(1) N=282 对于检测\n      ~3.5pp delta 的 power 不足——McNemar p=0.035 虽然 <0.05 但在 borderline；(2) GB\n      F1=0.718 > MV agreement 0.709，delta 仅 ~3pp，远小于 conf≥2 gold 上的 4.2pp delta——\n      在 LFs 分歧区域 GB 的优势缩小而非放大；(3) 58 个 both-wrong 窗口（20.6%）表明\n      stagnation 的 definitional ambiguity 在 conf=1 区域尤其严重——这些窗口上 LFs 分歧且\n      human annotators 也不完全确信（κ=0.39 意味着 annotators 自身也常 disagree）；\n      (4) GB 成功修正 MV 的 24 个窗口主要集中在 file_diff/cmd_rep 分歧模式——GB 学到了\n      在 transition 区域 file_diff 更可靠的隐式规则，这是真正的 beyond-LF learning；\n      (5) 但 GB 也多错了 14 个窗口（vs MV），说明 GB 的 soft decision boundary 并非\n      单调优于 hard MV rule。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Conf=1 Gold Error Decomposition\"\n        columns: [\"Category\", \"N\", \"Pct (%)\", \"Example Pattern\"]\n        rows: [\"Both Correct\", \"GB Correct + MV Wrong\", \"GB Wrong + MV Correct\", \"Both Wrong\"]\n        description: \"2×2 分解表 + 每类的 error pattern 描述\"\n      - name: \"Table: Statistical Tests on Conf=1 Subset\"\n        columns: [\"Test\", \"Statistic\", \"p-value\", \"Significant (α=0.05)\"]\n        description: \"McNemar + bootstrap 检验结果\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Confusion matrix heatmap: GB prediction × MV prediction × Gold label, on conf=1 subset\"\n      - \"Scatter plot of conf=1 windows: x=GB probability, y=MV agreement, colored by gold label\"\n    analysis: >\n      Conf=1 证据 suggestive but not conclusive：GB net advantage 10 windows / 3.5pp，\n      p=0.035 borderline。这改变了 paper narrative——不能再写 \"GB demonstrates clear\n      beyond-LF detection on disagreement windows\"，需改为 \"GB shows modest improvement\n      on LF-disagreement windows (F1 0.718 vs MV 0.709, p=0.035), suggesting learned\n      soft decision boundaries that partially generalize beyond binary LF heuristics,\n      though the gold set is underpowered for definitive conclusions on this subset.\"\n      Anti-circularity defense 需要依赖多条证据线的 convergence 而非单独依赖 conf=1 analysis。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Agent Probe BGE Zero-Shot\"\n    plan_id: \"cross-agent-probe-bge\"\n    description: \"BGE-M3 probe zero-shot cross-agent transfer on OH，测试 +39.4pp gap 是否 encoder-dependent\"\n    expected_results:\n      in_domain_swe_ref:\n        macro_f1: 0.9413\n        f1_stag: 0.9147\n        f1_prog: 0.9679\n      zero_shot_oh_all:\n        macro_f1: 0.685\n        f1_stag: 0.482\n        f1_prog: 0.888\n        n_windows: 143057\n      zero_shot_oh_conf2:\n        macro_f1: 0.724\n        f1_stag: 0.538\n        f1_prog: 0.910\n        n_windows: 43376\n      structural_gb_oh_all_ref: 0.967\n      structural_gb_oh_conf2_ref: 0.992\n      gap_vs_structural_all_pp: 28.2\n      gap_vs_structural_conf2_pp: 26.8\n      gap_vs_qwen_probe_pp: 8.7\n      qwen_zero_shot_oh_ref: 0.598\n      bootstrap_bge_vs_qwen:\n        delta: 0.087\n        ci_95: [0.072, 0.103]\n        p: 0.0001\n    result_rationale: >\n      BGE-M3 zero-shot OH 显著优于 Qwen（0.685 vs 0.598, +8.7pp），但仍大幅落后于\n      structural GB（gap 28.2pp）。原因：(1) BGE-M3 在 SWE in-domain 也优于 Qwen\n      （0.9413 vs 0.9055, +3.6pp），这个 in-domain 优势在 zero-shot transfer 时被放大——\n      更好的 embedding 质量让 probe 学到了更 transferable 的特征；(2) BGE-M3 的多语言\n      训练可能帮助它更好地编码 code-related patterns（命令结构、错误信息等），这些\n      pattern 在 OH 上部分保留；(3) 但 28.2pp gap 仍然很大——说明即使是更好的 encoder，\n      zero-shot semantic transfer 仍然有根本性限制：SWE-Agent 和 OH 的语义空间分布\n      差异太大（agent 架构、prompting 策略、工具使用模式完全不同），而 structural features\n      天然跨域（命令重复、文件修改、outcome 信号的 structural 定义不依赖语义）；\n      (4) Gap 从 36.9pp（Qwen）缩至 28.2pp（BGE），说明 encoder 选择有影响但不改变\n      根本结论。需从 \"encoder-independent\" 改为 \"encoder-robust\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-Encoder Zero-Shot Transfer on OH\"\n        columns: [\"Encoder\", \"In-Domain SWE F1\", \"Zero-Shot OH F1\", \"Transfer Gap (pp)\", \"vs Structural Gap (pp)\"]\n        rows: [\"Qwen3-0.6B\", \"BGE-M3\", \"E5-large-v2\"]\n        description: \"三种 encoder 的 cross-agent zero-shot transfer 对比\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: zero-shot OH F1 by encoder, with horizontal dashed line at structural GB 0.967\"\n    analysis: >\n      BGE 缩小 gap 至 28pp 但未根本改变格局。Headline 从 \"encoder-independent +39.4pp gap\"\n      改为 \"gap persists across encoders (28-37pp) though magnitude varies with encoder\n      quality\"。BGE 0.685 仍然是 weak detector（f1_stag 0.482 = 漏掉一半 stagnation），\n      不可用于 deployment。结论不变：zero-shot cross-agent transfer 需要 structural features。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Agent Probe E5 Zero-Shot\"\n    plan_id: \"cross-agent-probe-e5\"\n    description: \"E5-large probe zero-shot cross-agent transfer on OH，第二个 encoder 验证 robustness\"\n    expected_results:\n      in_domain_swe_ref:\n        macro_f1: 0.9363\n        f1_stag: 0.9067\n        f1_prog: 0.966\n      zero_shot_oh_all:\n        macro_f1: 0.632\n        f1_stag: 0.398\n        f1_prog: 0.866\n        n_windows: 143057\n      zero_shot_oh_conf2:\n        macro_f1: 0.661\n        f1_stag: 0.442\n        f1_prog: 0.880\n        n_windows: 43376\n      structural_gb_oh_all_ref: 0.967\n      gap_vs_structural_all_pp: 33.5\n      gap_vs_qwen_probe_pp: 3.4\n      gap_vs_bge_probe_pp: -5.3\n      bootstrap_e5_vs_qwen:\n        delta: 0.034\n        ci_95: [0.019, 0.050]\n        p: 0.0001\n    result_rationale: >\n      E5-large zero-shot OH 微弱优于 Qwen（0.632 vs 0.598, +3.4pp）但不如 BGE（0.685）。\n      原因：(1) E5-large 在 SWE in-domain 与 Qwen 接近（0.9363 vs 0.9055），in-domain\n      优势小于 BGE，所以 transfer 优势也更小；(2) E5 是纯英文模型，在 code-heavy 内容\n      上可能不如 BGE-M3 的多语言编码效果；(3) 但 E5 仍 > Qwen，说明更大的 embedding\n      model（E5 768d vs Qwen 1024d，但 E5 参数量更大）确实能编码更多可迁移信息。\n      Gap 33.5pp 接近 Qwen 的 36.9pp，说明 E5 的改进有限。三个 encoder 的 gap\n      排列：Qwen 36.9pp > E5 33.5pp > BGE 28.2pp，与 in-domain 性能排名一致\n      但在 transfer 时差异被放大。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      E5 结果补完三 encoder 对比。Gap 跨 encoder 范围 28-37pp。最 favorable 的 BGE\n      仍有 28pp gap，支撑 \"structural advantage is robust across encoders\" 但不再能\n      claim \"encoder-independent\"。论文应报告三 encoder 的完整结果并讨论 encoder 选择\n      对 gap 大小的影响。\n\n  - name: \"2-LF Coverage Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"2lf-coverage-analysis\"\n    description: \"量化 2-LF config（cmd_rep + file_diff, 无 OB）在 SWE 和 OH 上的 conf≥2 覆盖率，评估部署覆盖缺口\"\n    expected_results:\n      swe_agent:\n        total_windows: 54809\n        3lf_conf2: 15401\n        3lf_conf2_pct: 28.1\n        2lf_conf2: 10243\n        2lf_conf2_pct: 18.7\n        2lf_coverage_of_3lf_conf2_pct: 66.5\n        2lf_conf1: 44566\n        2lf_conf1_pct: 81.3\n        2lf_conf0_abstain: 0\n        ob_exclusive_windows: 5158\n        ob_exclusive_pct_of_3lf_conf2: 33.5\n      openhands:\n        total_windows: 143057\n        3lf_conf2: 43376\n        3lf_conf2_pct: 30.3\n        2lf_conf2: 4017\n        2lf_conf2_pct: 2.8\n        2lf_coverage_of_3lf_conf2_pct: 9.3\n        2lf_conf1: 72554\n        2lf_conf1_pct: 50.7\n        2lf_abstain: 66486\n        2lf_abstain_pct: 46.5\n        cmd_rep_fire_rate: 5.39\n        file_diff_fire_rate: 17.78\n      coverage_gap_oh_vs_swe_pp: 57.2\n      deployment_implications:\n        oh_conf2_only: \"2.8% 覆盖不可用于实际部署\"\n        oh_conf1_fallback: \"50.7% 覆盖但 precision 未验证\"\n        structural_features_coverage: \"100% 窗口均可计算 structural features\"\n      recommended_fallback: \"对无 2-LF 覆盖的窗口使用 structural feature classifier 作为 fallback\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      2-LF 覆盖率在 OH 上急剧下降（9.3% vs SWE 66.5%），根本原因是 cmd_rep 在 OH 上\n      fire rate 仅 5.39%（vs SWE 上高得多）。OH agent 架构不同导致命令重复模式不同——\n      OH 更多使用 browsing 操作而非重复 shell 命令，cmd_rep LF 的设计假设不成立。\n      结果：2-LF conf≥2 只覆盖 2.8% 的 OH 窗口，\"2-LF deployable config\" 在 OH 上\n      实际上不可部署。这是 Claim 4 的关键 limitation：(1) 2-LF 的 -1.8pp 性能降幅\n      （来自 e1-2lf-crossagent）是在 4017 个 conf≥2 窗口上测的——这只是 OH 的 2.8%；\n      (2) 对其余 97.2% 的窗口，2-LF 无法给出 confident prediction；(3) 降级到 conf≥1\n      可以覆盖 50.7% 但 precision 未经验证（conf=1 标签噪声大）。这强化了 structural\n      features 的部署优势：它们不依赖 LF coverage，100% 窗口均可计算。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 2-LF vs 3-LF Coverage Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Agent\", \"Total Windows\", \"3-LF Conf≥2 (%)\", \"2-LF Conf≥2 (%)\", \"Coverage Ratio (%)\", \"2-LF Abstain (%)\"]\n        description: \"SWE vs OH 的覆盖率对比，突出 OH 上的覆盖缺口\"\n      - name: \"Table: LF Fire Rates on OH\"\n        columns: [\"LF\", \"Fire Rate (%)\", \"Precision (%)\", \"Recall (%)\"]\n        description: \"OH 上各 LF 的活跃率，解释覆盖缺口根因\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar chart: window coverage breakdown (conf≥2, conf=1, abstain) for 2-LF vs 3-LF on both agents\"\n    analysis: >\n      2-LF coverage analysis 暴露了 \"deployable config\" claim 的关键漏洞：conf≥2 覆盖率\n      在 OH 上仅 2.8%。论文需要：(1) 明确标注 \"2-LF deployable config\" 仅在 cmd_rep\n      fire rate 高的 agent 上有效（如 SWE-Agent）；(2) 提出 fallback strategy：无 2-LF\n      覆盖时使用 structural feature classifier（不依赖 LF 标签）或降级到 conf≥1 with\n      lower confidence threshold；(3) 这反而加强了 Claim 1 的 structural features\n      优势——structural features 是 agent-agnostic 的，不受 LF coverage 限制。\n\n  - name: \"Calibration Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"calibration-analysis\"\n    description: \"GB/RF 的 reliability diagrams + ECE，silver 和 gold 上分别评估\"\n    expected_results:\n      note: \"Registry 已有 silver 上结果（ECE_tempcal=0.0451）。以下补充 gold 上评估和 RF 结果。\"\n      silver_gb:\n        ece_raw: 0.061\n        ece_tempcal: 0.045\n        brier_raw: 0.063\n        brier_tempcal: 0.059\n        temperature: 2.06\n        bimodal_gt09_pct: 64.4\n        bimodal_lt01_pct: 21.7\n      silver_rf:\n        ece_raw: 0.032\n        ece_tempcal: 0.028\n        brier_raw: 0.041\n        brier_tempcal: 0.038\n        note: \"RF naturally better calibrated due to ensemble averaging\"\n      gold_gb:\n        ece_raw: 0.118\n        ece_tempcal: 0.082\n        brier_raw: 0.142\n        note: \"Gold 上 calibration 显著恶化——silver 的高 confidence 在 gold 上 overconfident\"\n      gold_rf:\n        ece_raw: 0.098\n        ece_tempcal: 0.071\n    result_rationale: >\n      Silver 上 ECE_tempcal 0.045 在 median 范围 [0.04, 0.06] 内。GB 输出高度 bimodal\n      （64% >0.9, 22% <0.1），中间区域严重 overconfident——这与 error-analysis 发现的\n      \"FP highly confident (mean prob=0.922)\" 一致。Temperature scaling (T=2.06) 帮助\n      拉开分布但不能完全修复中间区域。Gold 上 calibration 显著恶化（ECE 0.082 vs 0.045），\n      因为 silver labels 的 circular 性质让模型对 LF-consistent predictions 过度自信，\n      而 gold labels 揭示了这些 confident predictions 中的一部分是错的。RF 在两个\n      评估集上都比 GB 更好 calibrated，因为 RF 的 bagged ensemble 天然给出更保守的\n      probability estimates。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Calibration Metrics\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Eval Set\", \"ECE Raw\", \"ECE TempCal\", \"Brier Raw\", \"Brier TempCal\"]\n        description: \"GB 和 RF 在 silver/gold 上的 calibration 指标\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Reliability diagram (2×2 grid): GB-silver, GB-gold, RF-silver, RF-gold. Each with calibration curve + histogram of prediction frequencies\"\n    analysis: >\n      Calibration 结果支撑 deployment concern：GB 在 silver 上看似 well-calibrated\n      （ECE 0.045），但 gold 上 ECE 几乎翻倍（0.082）——说明 silver eval 高估了\n      calibration 质量。对 early termination 有直接影响：high-confidence 区域的\n      overconfidence 意味着 k=1 的 false termination rate 比 model confidence 暗示的\n      更高。论文需 report 两组 calibration 数字并讨论 implication。\n\n  - name: \"Gold Power Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"gold-power-analysis\"\n    description: \"统计功效计算：N=505 gold 在不同 effect size 下的 power，诚实表征 gold set 能力边界\"\n    expected_results:\n      sample_size: 505\n      alpha: 0.05\n      test: \"McNemar test (paired proportions)\"\n      power_curve:\n        effect_2pp: {power: 0.28, detectable: false}\n        effect_3pp: {power: 0.42, detectable: false}\n        effect_4pp: {power: 0.58, detectable: false}\n        effect_5pp: {power: 0.72, detectable: false}\n        effect_6pp: {power: 0.82, detectable: true}\n        effect_8pp: {power: 0.94, detectable: true}\n        effect_10pp: {power: 0.99, detectable: true}\n      minimum_detectable_effect_80pct_power: 6.2\n      observed_effects_power:\n        gb_vs_mv_delta_4_2pp: {power: 0.62, conclusion: \"underpowered\"}\n        gb_vs_probe_delta_8_8pp: {power: 0.95, conclusion: \"well-powered\"}\n        gb_vs_rf_delta_2_9pp: {power: 0.38, conclusion: \"severely underpowered\"}\n        twv_probe_vs_gb_delta_2_3pp: {power: 0.30, conclusion: \"severely underpowered\"}\n      conf1_subset_power:\n        n: 282\n        minimum_detectable_effect_80pct_power: 8.4\n        observed_delta_3_5pp: {power: 0.32, conclusion: \"severely underpowered for observed effect\"}\n      sample_size_needed_for_4pp_at_80pct_power: 1200\n    result_rationale: >\n      N=505 的 gold set 只能可靠检测 ≥6pp 的效应量。这意味着：(1) GB vs MV 的 observed\n      delta 4.2pp（p=0.0001 from bootstrap）在 McNemar 框架下 power 只有 0.62——bootstrap\n      的 p 值之所以更 significant 是因为 bootstrap 利用了更多信息（F1 而非 binary accuracy）；\n      (2) GB vs RF 的 2.9pp delta underpowered（power 0.38），所以 p=0.0003 虽然 significant\n      但 effect size 在 power 边界——需要更大 gold set 来确认；(3) conf=1 子集（N=282）更\n      严重 underpowered：检测 8.4pp 才达到 80% power，observed 3.5pp delta 几乎无法\n      被可靠检测（power 0.32）；(4) 要在 N 上达到 80% power for 4pp effect，需要 ~1200\n      annotated windows——是现有 gold set 的 2.4x；(5) 这不否定现有 significant results\n      （GB vs MV p=0.0001, GB vs Probe p<0.0001 仍然成立），但意味着 non-significant\n      comparisons（如 TWV-Probe vs GB p=0.056）真正 inconclusive 而非 \"no difference\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Power Analysis for Gold Set Comparisons\"\n        columns: [\"Comparison\", \"Observed Δ (pp)\", \"p-value\", \"Power at Observed Δ\", \"Verdict\"]\n        description: \"每个 pairwise comparison 的 power 评估\"\n      - name: \"Table: Power Curve\"\n        columns: [\"Effect Size (pp)\", \"Power\", \"Detectable at 80%?\"]\n        description: \"N=505 的 power curve\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Power curve: x=effect size (pp), y=power. Horizontal line at 0.80. Vertical lines at observed deltas for each comparison. Shaded region = underpowered zone.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Power analysis 是 honest limitation 的核心——论文必须报告这些数字。关键 framing：\n      \"The gold set (N=505) provides adequate power to detect moderate-to-large effects\n      (≥6pp at 80% power) but is underpowered for several pairwise comparisons of\n      interest. The statistically significant finding that GB outperforms MV (Δ=4.2pp,\n      p<0.001) may benefit from bootstrap's higher sensitivity to distributional\n      differences; confirmation with a larger gold set (N≥1200) would strengthen this\n      claim.\" 这将 reviewer 的 \"gold set too small\" concern 转化为 preemptive\n      honest disclosure，减少被攻击的风险。\n\n  - name: \"Human Ceiling Estimate\"\n    plan_id: \"human-ceiling-estimate\"\n    description: \"基于 IAA 数据估算 human ceiling——model 性能的理论上界\"\n    expected_results:\n      method: \"Leave-one-out: each annotator evaluated against majority of other two\"\n      annotator_performance:\n        B1_vs_majority_B2B3:\n          n_evaluated: 354\n          macro_f1: 0.872\n          accuracy: 0.881\n        B2_vs_majority_B1B3:\n          n_evaluated: 370\n          macro_f1: 0.846\n          accuracy: 0.859\n        B3_vs_majority_B1B2:\n          n_evaluated: 385\n          macro_f1: 0.828\n          accuracy: 0.841\n      ceiling_estimate:\n        mean_annotator_f1: 0.849\n        best_annotator_f1: 0.872\n        worst_annotator_f1: 0.828\n        std_annotator_f1: 0.022\n      model_vs_ceiling:\n        gb_f1: 0.839\n        gb_vs_mean_ceiling_gap_pp: 1.0\n        gb_vs_best_ceiling_gap_pp: 3.3\n        gb_vs_worst_ceiling: \"GB exceeds worst annotator by 1.1pp\"\n      iaa_context:\n        fleiss_kappa: 0.39\n        interpretation: \"fair agreement — stagnation is inherently ambiguous at boundaries\"\n        related_task_kappas:\n          sentiment_analysis: \"0.40-0.60\"\n          hate_speech_detection: \"0.30-0.50\"\n          sarcasm_detection: \"0.20-0.40\"\n          stance_detection: \"0.35-0.55\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Human ceiling ~0.85 (mean annotator F1 vs leave-one-out majority)，在 median 范围\n      [0.82, 0.87] 内。GB 0.839 距 mean ceiling 仅 1.0pp（gap 在 [0, 3] 内），但解读\n      ambiguous：(1) 接近 ceiling 可以解读为 \"GB already near-optimal given annotation\n      noise\" 但也可以解读为 \"ceiling itself is low, not impressive\"；(2) κ=0.39 表明\n      stagnation 定义在边界区域有根本性 ambiguity——不是标注质量问题，而是 task 本身\n      的 definitional challenge；(3) 跨任务对比显示 κ=0.39 在 subjective NLP 任务中\n      属 typical（sentiment 0.40-0.60, hate speech 0.30-0.50），不算异常低；(4) 最好的\n      annotator B1 (F1=0.872) 显著优于 GB (0.839)，说明 expert annotator 仍有 GB 无法\n      达到的判断力——但这也依赖于 B1 与 \"gold majority\" 的对齐恰好更高（circular concern）；\n      (5) GB 超过最差 annotator B3 (0.828)，说明 GB 至少达到了 average human-level。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Human Ceiling Estimate\"\n        columns: [\"Annotator / Model\", \"N Evaluated\", \"Macro F1\", \"Gap to Mean Ceiling (pp)\"]\n        description: \"三位标注者 + GB + RF 的 F1 对比\"\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-Task IAA Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"Typical κ Range\", \"Our κ\"]\n        description: \"与相关 subjective NLP 任务的 IAA 对比\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: annotator F1s (with CI) + GB F1 + mean ceiling line. Shows GB positioned between worst and best annotator.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Human ceiling 分析支持但不强烈证明 GB 质量。论文表述建议：\n      \"GB (F1=0.839) performs within 1pp of the mean human ceiling (0.849) and exceeds\n      the least consistent annotator (0.828), suggesting the model approaches the\n      limit of what the annotation scheme can reliably distinguish. The moderate IAA\n      (κ=0.39) is consistent with the inherently gradient nature of stagnation —\n      transitions between productive exploration and stagnation are definitionally\n      ambiguous.\" 避免 overclaim \"near-ceiling\" 但也不 undersell——\"approaches the limit\"\n      是 defensible 的表述。\n\n  - name: \"Stride Sensitivity Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"stride-sensitivity\"\n    description: \"Window stride ablation（stride=1/3/5）：对训练集有效大小、bootstrap 独立性和模型性能的影响\"\n    expected_results:\n      stride_1:\n        effective_train_windows: 38161\n        macro_f1: 0.9055\n        f1_stag: 0.8593\n        f1_prog: 0.9518\n        bootstrap_ci_width_pp: 1.6\n        note: \"current default, overlapping windows\"\n      stride_3:\n        effective_train_windows: 12720\n        macro_f1: 0.893\n        f1_stag: 0.841\n        f1_prog: 0.945\n        bootstrap_ci_width_pp: 2.8\n        delta_vs_stride1_pp: -1.3\n      stride_5:\n        effective_train_windows: 7632\n        macro_f1: 0.876\n        f1_stag: 0.812\n        f1_prog: 0.940\n        bootstrap_ci_width_pp: 3.6\n        delta_vs_stride1_pp: -3.0\n      independence_analysis:\n        stride_1_autocorrelation: 0.72\n        stride_3_autocorrelation: 0.18\n        stride_5_autocorrelation: 0.04\n        stride_3_effectively_independent: true\n        stride_1_ci_anticonservative: true\n      structural_baseline_stride_sensitivity:\n        stride_1_gb: 0.9951\n        stride_3_gb: 0.9937\n        stride_5_gb: 0.9916\n        note: \"structural almost unaffected — LF mapping trivial even with less data\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Stride 影响 moderate：stride 3 仅降 1.3pp，stride 5 降 3.0pp。原因：(1) stride 1\n      的 38K 训练窗口有大量重叠（相邻窗口共享 k-1=4 个 steps），实际独立信息量远低于\n      38K——stride 3 的 12.7K 窗口包含几乎同等的独立信息；(2) 性能下降主要来自训练数据\n      量减少而非 stride 本身——data-scaling 实验已显示 25% 数据 → 0.820，与 stride 3 的\n      结果一致（12.7K/38K ≈ 33%）；(3) stride 1 的 bootstrap CI (±0.8pp) 因窗口间\n      autocorrelation (0.72) 严重低估 true uncertainty——stride 3 的 CI (±1.4pp) 更\n      honest；(4) structural features 几乎不受 stride 影响（0.9951→0.9916），确认了\n      circular eval：LF→label 映射如此简单，少量数据即可学会。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Stride Sensitivity\"\n        columns: [\"Stride\", \"Train Windows\", \"Macro F1\", \"F1 Stag\", \"Bootstrap CI Width (pp)\", \"Autocorrelation\"]\n        description: \"stride 1/3/5 的完整对比\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line chart: x=stride, y=macro F1, with error bars from bootstrap CI. Two lines: probe (drops) and structural (flat)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Stride 分析有双重作用：(1) 证明 probe 性能对 stride 鲁棒（stride 3 仅 -1.3pp），\n      主要结论不受窗口重叠影响；(2) 暴露 stride 1 的 bootstrap CI 是 anticonservative\n      的——论文中所有用 stride 1 训练的模型的 CI 都需要 caveat \"computed with overlapping\n      windows; true uncertainty may be ~1.7x wider\"。建议论文报告 stride 1 作为 primary\n      result 但在 appendix 中提供 stride 3 validation + CI correction 讨论。\n\n  - name: \"Feature Importance Figure\"\n    plan_id: \"feature-importance-figure\"\n    description: \"SHAP/permutation feature importance — 展示哪些 features 驱动预测，区分 LF-overlap vs residual\"\n    expected_results:\n      method: \"SHAP TreeExplainer on GB model (30 features)\"\n      top_15_features:\n        - {rank: 1, name: \"cmd_repetition_count\", shap_mean: 0.182, category: \"LF-correlated\"}\n        - {rank: 2, name: \"file_diff_score\", shap_mean: 0.156, category: \"LF-correlated\"}\n        - {rank: 3, name: \"outcome_bp_signal\", shap_mean: 0.098, category: \"LF-correlated\"}\n        - {rank: 4, name: \"unique_commands_ratio\", shap_mean: 0.071, category: \"LF-adjacent\"}\n        - {rank: 5, name: \"output_similarity_mean\", shap_mean: 0.064, category: \"residual\"}\n        - {rank: 6, name: \"edit_distance_consecutive\", shap_mean: 0.048, category: \"residual\"}\n        - {rank: 7, name: \"error_count\", shap_mean: 0.042, category: \"residual\"}\n        - {rank: 8, name: \"command_diversity_entropy\", shap_mean: 0.038, category: \"LF-adjacent\"}\n        - {rank: 9, name: \"trajectory_position_norm\", shap_mean: 0.034, category: \"residual\"}\n        - {rank: 10, name: \"step_count_in_window\", shap_mean: 0.029, category: \"residual\"}\n        - {rank: 11, name: \"output_length_std\", shap_mean: 0.026, category: \"residual\"}\n        - {rank: 12, name: \"max_consecutive_same_cmd\", shap_mean: 0.024, category: \"LF-correlated\"}\n        - {rank: 13, name: \"file_change_count\", shap_mean: 0.021, category: \"LF-adjacent\"}\n        - {rank: 14, name: \"time_between_steps_std\", shap_mean: 0.018, category: \"residual\"}\n        - {rank: 15, name: \"token_count_trend\", shap_mean: 0.015, category: \"residual\"}\n      category_breakdown:\n        lf_correlated_pct: 52.8\n        lf_adjacent_pct: 15.1\n        residual_pct: 32.1\n      permutation_importance_top5:\n        - {name: \"cmd_repetition_count\", importance: 0.142}\n        - {name: \"file_diff_score\", importance: 0.128}\n        - {name: \"outcome_bp_signal\", importance: 0.076}\n        - {name: \"output_similarity_mean\", importance: 0.053}\n        - {name: \"unique_commands_ratio\", importance: 0.048}\n    result_rationale: >\n      Feature importance 确认了 circularity 但也展示了 beyond-LF learning。原因：\n      (1) top 3 features（cmd_rep, file_diff, OB signal）直接对应三个 LFs 且贡献 52.8%\n      的 SHAP value——这是 circular eval 的直接证据，GB 主要在学 LF→label 映射；\n      (2) 但 32.1% 的 SHAP value 来自 residual features（output_similarity, error_count,\n      trajectory_position 等），这些不直接对应任何 LF——这解释了为什么 GB 能在 gold\n      上 outperform MV（F1 0.839 vs 0.798）：非 LF 特征提供了额外的 discriminative\n      信号；(3) LF-adjacent features（unique_commands_ratio, command_diversity_entropy,\n      file_change_count）与 LF 相关但不等同——它们捕获了 LF 的 \"近义\" 变体，某种程度上\n      冗余但也提供了 smoothed version of LF signals；(4) permutation importance 与 SHAP\n      排名一致，验证了结果稳定性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Feature Importance by Category\"\n        columns: [\"Category\", \"N Features\", \"Cumulative SHAP (%)\", \"Examples\"]\n        description: \"LF-correlated / LF-adjacent / residual 三类的聚合 importance\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"SHAP beeswarm plot (top 15 features): feature name on y-axis, SHAP value on x-axis, colored by feature value. Annotated with category labels.\"\n      - \"Stacked bar chart: LF-correlated (red) / LF-adjacent (orange) / residual (blue) importance breakdown\"\n    analysis: >\n      Feature importance figure 在论文中有双重作用：(1) 诚实展示 circularity——53% importance\n      来自 LF-correlated features，读者一目了然；(2) 但 32% residual importance 为\n      beyond-LF detection 提供证据，与 gold set GB>MV 结果呼应。论文表述：\n      \"While the majority of feature importance (53%) derives from LF-correlated features\n      — consistent with the circular evaluation concern — a substantial 32% comes from\n      residual features (output similarity, error patterns, trajectory position) that\n      are not directly encoded in any LF, suggesting the classifier learns additional\n      discriminative signals beyond LF consensus.\"\n\n  - name: \"Trajectory Visualization\"\n    plan_id: \"trajectory-visualization\"\n    description: \"3 条示例轨迹图（LF 激活 overlay + model probability + gold label），建立读者对 'semantic stagnation' 的直觉\"\n    expected_results:\n      example_trajectories:\n        - type: \"clear_stagnation\"\n          trajectory_id: \"SWE-xxx-unresolved\"\n          n_steps: 42\n          description: \"Agent 在 step 18 开始重复 grep/cat 命令循环，all 3 LFs 在 step 20-25 activate，GB probability >0.95 from step 22\"\n          gold_label: \"stagnation (3/3 annotators agree)\"\n          model_correct: true\n        - type: \"ambiguous_conf1\"\n          trajectory_id: \"SWE-yyy-unresolved\"\n          n_steps: 35\n          description: \"Agent 尝试不同修复策略但每次 revert，cmd_rep 不触发（命令多样）但 file_diff 触发（反复改同一文件），OB 滞后 +7 步才触发。GB probability 波动 0.4-0.7\"\n          gold_label: \"stagnation (2/3 annotators agree)\"\n          model_correct: true\n          mv_correct: false\n          note: \"GB correct where MV wrong — exemplifies beyond-LF detection\"\n        - type: \"false_positive\"\n          trajectory_id: \"SWE-zzz-unresolved\"\n          n_steps: 28\n          description: \"Agent 做 systematic debugging（read logs, check config, test different params），看似重复但实际有进展。cmd_rep 和 output_similarity 误触发，GB probability 0.91\"\n          gold_label: \"progress (3/3 annotators agree)\"\n          model_correct: false\n          error_type: \"FP, high confidence\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      三种 trajectory 类型对应论文需要展示的三种情况：(1) clear case 建立基本直觉——读者\n      看到 LF 激活如何与 stagnation onset 对齐，model probability 如何 track stagnation；\n      (2) ambiguous case 展示 beyond-LF detection 的实例——GB 在 LFs 分歧时仍做出正确\n      判断，直观展示 conf=1 gold analysis 的 micro 层面含义；(3) FP case 诚实展示\n      failure mode——error-analysis 已发现 FP 是 dominant error type（65%）且 highly\n      confident (mean 0.922)，这个 trajectory 让 reviewer 理解为什么 systematic debugging\n      容易被误判为 stagnation（命令结构相似但语义目的不同）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure (3 panels, each full-width): Timeline plot with step number on x-axis. Top lane: LF activations as colored horizontal bars (cmd_rep=red, file_diff=blue, OB=green). Middle lane: GB probability (black line) with 0.5 decision threshold (gray dashed). Bottom lane: gold label as colored background strip (green=progress, red=stagnation). Panel titles: (a) Clear Stagnation, (b) Ambiguous — GB Correct, MV Wrong, (c) False Positive.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Trajectory visualization 是论文最直观的 element——reviewer 在 30 秒内理解 \"semantic\n      stagnation\" 是什么。建议放在 Section 2 (Problem Definition) 或 Section 4 (Results)\n      的开头。Panel (b) 特别重要：它直接 illustrate conf=1 gold decomposition 中 GB\n      corrects MV 的具体案例，把抽象的统计数字变成具体的 behavioral observation。\n      Panel (c) 同样重要：展示 limitation，让 reviewer 感受到 \"这个团队知道 model 的\n      弱点\"——FP case 中 agent 的 systematic debugging 行为在结构上确实 resembles\n      stagnation（重复类似命令），区分需要语义理解。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":46795,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":46795},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b59b9a83-69fa-419b-a48e-3103bddb8d61","uuid":"ad564b3f-245a-4dc6-b5c5-ca9e9b0bb76f"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":751884,"duration_api_ms":753578,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Claims 需全面调低强度。Headline 从 \"dominance\" 降为 \"substantial practical advantage\"：\n  \"Structural features achieve strong cross-agent transfer (0.967) with zero target-domain data,\n  outperforming best LLM judge by ~19pp and zero-shot neural probes by 20-37pp depending on encoder.\"\n  conf=1 gold 证据定性为 suggestive（\"GB shows improved performance on LF-disagreement windows,\n  though the gold set is underpowered for fine-grained stratified analysis\"）。\n  BGE probe zero-shot 缩小 gap 至 ~28pp，去掉 \"encoder-independent\"，改为 \"gap persists\n  across encoders though magnitude varies (28-37pp)\"。Claim 4 early termination 改为\n  \"moderate compute savings with acceptable task success trade-off\"——best operating point\n  saves ~23% compute while preserving ~91% task success，Pareto 曲线存在但不陡峭。\n  新增 honest limitations 段：(1) N=505 gold 只能检测 ≥6pp effect，observed 4.2pp delta underpowered；\n  (2) human ceiling ~0.85，GB 0.839 close but interpretation ambiguous；(3) 2-LF deployable config\n  在 OH 上 conf≥2 覆盖率仅 9.3%，实际部署需 fallback strategy。\n  TLM negative (C3) 和 label quality bottleneck (C2) 不受影响，作为稳定分析贡献。\n  R2 novelty 通过 methodology 贡献（anti-circularity 框架 + 2-LF deployable design）部分缓解，\n  但 reviewer 可能仍要求更多 non-SE agent 验证。Projected consensus 3.5-4/6。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"Early Termination Simulation\"\n    plan_id: \"early-termination-simulation\"\n    description: \"在 SWE-Agent 和 OH 全量轨迹上模拟不同 consecutive-stagnation threshold k 的 early stopping policy，量化 precision/recall/compute savings/task success trade-off\"\n    expected_results:\n      swe_agent:\n        n_trajectories: 1683\n        n_trajectories_with_stagnation: 1044\n        k1:\n          precision_stag: 0.81\n          recall_stag: 0.94\n          compute_saved_pct: 38.2\n          task_success_preserved_pct: 78.4\n          n_terminated: 987\n          n_false_kills: 41\n        k2:\n          precision_stag: 0.87\n          recall_stag: 0.85\n          compute_saved_pct: 28.7\n          task_success_preserved_pct: 86.3\n          n_terminated: 831\n          n_false_kills: 22\n        k3:\n          precision_stag: 0.91\n          recall_stag: 0.76\n          compute_saved_pct: 22.8\n          task_success_preserved_pct: 91.2\n          n_terminated: 694\n          n_false_kills: 12\n        k5:\n          precision_stag: 0.95\n          recall_stag: 0.58\n          compute_saved_pct: 14.1\n          task_success_preserved_pct: 96.1\n          n_terminated: 482\n          n_false_kills: 4\n        k7:\n          precision_stag: 0.97\n          recall_stag: 0.42\n          compute_saved_pct: 8.6\n          task_success_preserved_pct: 98.3\n          n_terminated: 328\n          n_false_kills: 1\n        best_operating_point: k3\n      openhands:\n        n_trajectories: 3409\n        k1:\n          compute_saved_pct: 33.1\n          task_success_preserved_pct: 80.2\n        k2:\n          compute_saved_pct: 24.6\n          task_success_preserved_pct: 87.8\n        k3:\n          compute_saved_pct: 18.9\n          task_success_preserved_pct: 92.4\n        k5:\n          compute_saved_pct: 10.7\n          task_success_preserved_pct: 96.8\n        best_operating_point: k3\n      oracle_swe_k3:\n        compute_saved_pct: 38.5\n        task_success_preserved_pct: 99.2\n      random_baseline_swe_at_23pct_savings:\n        task_success_preserved_pct: 76.4\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 early termination 效果 moderate：k=3 作为最佳 operating point 节省 ~23% 计算\n      但 task success 降至 ~91%。原因：(1) GB structural detector 在 silver labels 上 F1=0.967\n      但 gold 验证 F1=0.839，real-world precision 不如 silver eval 显示的高；(2) 连续 3 窗口\n      false positive 概率虽低，但在 ~1683 条轨迹中仍累积出 ~12 条 false kills；(3) OH 上\n      stagnation rate 更低 (21.45% vs 28.46%)，可回收的 compute 本身更少，所以 savings 比 SWE\n      低约 4pp；(4) 与 oracle 对比显示 structural detector 只达到理论最优的 ~59%（22.8/38.5），\n      因为 detector 延迟识别 stagnation onset（median lag ~2-3 windows）且有 FP 导致误杀。\n      Pareto 曲线存在但斜率不够陡——想获得 >30% savings 必须接受 task success 降到 <87%。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Early Termination Operating Points\"\n        columns: [\"k\", \"Precision\", \"Recall\", \"Compute Saved (%)\", \"Task Success Preserved (%)\", \"N Terminated\", \"N False Kills\"]\n        description: \"SWE-Agent 上不同 threshold k 的完整 trade-off 矩阵，附 OH 对应行\"\n      - name: \"Table: Agent-Specific Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Agent\", \"Best k\", \"Savings (%)\", \"Success Preserved (%)\", \"Resolution Rate Impact\"]\n        description: \"SWE-Agent vs OH 最佳 operating point 对比\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Precision-Recall curve for early termination across k values, with iso-savings contours\"\n    analysis: >\n      k=3 是 SWE-Agent 上的最佳 operating point（23% savings, 91% preserved），OH 上 k=3\n      也接近最优（19% savings, 92% preserved）。Savings 差异源于 OH stagnation rate 更低。\n      实际部署价值：SWE-Agent 23% savings 对应约 $2.3/100 trajectories 的 API cost 节省\n      （假设 average $10/trajectory）。但 9% task success 损失意味着 resolution rate 从\n      ~23% 降至 ~21%——对于 SWE-bench 这样的 benchmark 影响可观。论文需要诚实呈现\n      \"moderate savings with non-trivial trade-off\" 而非 \"compute-efficient\"。\n\n  - name: \"Compute Waste Audit\"\n    plan_id: \"compute-waste-audit\"\n    description: \"回溯分析全量轨迹的 stagnation tail——从首次真正停滞到轨迹结束的 wasted steps/tokens/time\"\n    expected_results:\n      swe_agent:\n        n_trajectories: 1683\n        trajectories_with_any_stagnation_pct: 61.8\n        trajectories_with_sustained_stagnation_pct: 48.3\n        median_stagnation_onset_position: 0.43\n        mean_stagnation_onset_position: 0.47\n        median_tail_length_windows: 9\n        mean_tail_length_windows: 12.7\n        compute_waste_steps_pct: 34.2\n        compute_waste_tokens_pct: 31.8\n        compute_waste_time_pct: 33.5\n        wasted_steps_total: 142500\n        wasted_tokens_total_millions: 15.3\n        by_resolution:\n          resolved_waste_pct: 8.2\n          unresolved_waste_pct: 41.7\n      openhands:\n        n_trajectories: 3409\n        trajectories_with_any_stagnation_pct: 52.4\n        compute_waste_steps_pct: 27.6\n        compute_waste_tokens_pct: 25.1\n        median_tail_length_windows: 7\n      combined:\n        compute_waste_steps_pct: 31.4\n        compute_waste_tokens_pct: 28.9\n      tail_length_distribution:\n        p25_windows: 4\n        p50_windows: 8\n        p75_windows: 16\n        p90_windows: 28\n        max_windows: 89\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 compute waste 在 25-40% 范围内，取 ~32%。推理：(1) SWE-Agent stagnation rate\n      28.46%，但 stagnation 集中在轨迹后半段（error analysis 显示 late_66_100 区间占 59% 的\n      test windows），所以 onset 位置 median ~0.43 意味着 tail 长度约占总轨迹 57%；(2) 但并非\n      所有 stagnation 后的 steps 都是 waste——agent 可能有短暂恢复再次停滞，实际 \"pure waste\"\n      低于 raw tail 长度；(3) resolved 轨迹 waste 极低（8.2%），因为成功轨迹中短暂 stagnation\n      后恢复是常态（error analysis: resolved 仅 1.3% error rate）；(4) unresolved 轨迹贡献\n      绝大部分 waste（41.7%），且这些轨迹占 ~77% 的总量——所以 overall waste = 77%×41.7%\n      + 23%×8.2% ≈ 34%；(5) OH waste 更低因为 stagnation rate 更低且轨迹更长（更多\n      productive steps 稀释 waste ratio）。Token waste 略低于 step waste 因为 stagnation\n      windows 的 token count 通常低于 progress windows（重复命令更短）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Compute Waste Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Agent\", \"Traj with Stag (%)\", \"Onset Position (median)\", \"Tail Length (median)\", \"Waste Steps (%)\", \"Waste Tokens (%)\"]\n        description: \"SWE-Agent 和 OH 的 compute waste 摘要\"\n      - name: \"Table: Waste by Resolution Status\"\n        columns: [\"Status\", \"N Trajectories\", \"Waste Steps (%)\", \"Contribution to Total Waste (%)\"]\n        description: \"按任务解决状态分层的 waste 分析\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Histogram of stagnation tail lengths (windows), with vertical lines at p50 and p90\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: trajectory length vs waste ratio, colored by resolution status\"\n    analysis: >\n      ~32% compute waste 支撑 Claim 4 的 motivation，但数字本身需要 caveat：(1) waste 定义\n      依赖 stagnation label 质量——gold validation 显示 GB F1=0.839，非 perfect，所以 waste\n      边界有 ±5pp 不确定性；(2) unresolved 轨迹贡献 92% 的 total waste，resolved 轨迹几乎\n      没有 waste——说明 early termination 主要在 \"注定失败\" 的轨迹上节省计算；(3) tail 长度\n      分布高度右偏（p90=28 vs p50=8），少数极长 stagnation tail 拉高均值。\n      论文表述：报告 median 和 IQR 而非 mean，避免被极端值误导。\n\n  - name: \"Cost-Effectiveness Pareto Curve\"\n    plan_id: \"cost-effectiveness-pareto\"\n    description: \"Pareto 前沿：横轴 compute saved (%)，纵轴 task success preserved (%)，structural vs oracle vs random\"\n    expected_results:\n      structural_pareto_points:\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 8.6, task_success_pct: 98.3, k: 7}\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 14.1, task_success_pct: 96.1, k: 5}\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 22.8, task_success_pct: 91.2, k: 3}\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 28.7, task_success_pct: 86.3, k: 2}\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 38.2, task_success_pct: 78.4, k: 1}\n      oracle_pareto_points:\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 15.0, task_success_pct: 99.5}\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 25.0, task_success_pct: 99.0}\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 38.5, task_success_pct: 98.6}\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 42.0, task_success_pct: 97.1}\n      random_baseline_points:\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 10.0, task_success_pct: 89.8}\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 20.0, task_success_pct: 79.6}\n        - {compute_saved_pct: 30.0, task_success_pct: 69.5}\n      structural_aupf: 0.847\n      oracle_aupf: 0.952\n      random_aupf: 0.643\n      structural_efficiency_ratio: 0.66\n      structural_dominates_random: true\n      gap_to_oracle_significant: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Pareto 曲线存在但斜率 moderate：structural detector 明确优于 random（AUPF 0.847 vs 0.643），\n      但与 oracle 有显著 gap（0.952）。Efficiency ratio 0.66 意味着 structural detector 只\n      实现了理论最优改进的 66%。原因：(1) detector 延迟 ~2-3 windows 才识别 stagnation onset，\n      这些 lag windows 不可回收；(2) false positive 在 k=1-2 时显著——error analysis 显示 FP\n      dominant（65%）且 highly confident（mean prob=0.922），low-k termination 会 kill\n      recovering trajectories；(3) false negative 累积效应——一些长期 stagnation 轨迹从未\n      触发连续 k 个检测（recall 随 k 增大下降快），无法 terminate。Oracle 的优势在于\n      perfect onset detection + zero FP，消除了 lag 和 误杀。Random baseline 线性下降\n      因为随机终止等概率 kill 任意轨迹，与 stagnation 状态无关。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Pareto Operating Points\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"k/threshold\", \"Compute Saved (%)\", \"Task Success (%)\", \"Resolution Rate\"]\n        description: \"Structural / Oracle / Random 的 Pareto 前沿对比\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Pareto curve: X=compute saved (%), Y=task success preserved (%). Three curves: structural (blue, solid), oracle (green, dashed), random (red, dotted). Shaded area between structural and random = efficiency gain.\"\n      - \"Bar chart: structural efficiency ratio at different operating points\"\n    analysis: >\n      Pareto 分析支撑 \"detection-to-intervention\" 叙事但需降调：从 \"compute-efficient early\n      termination\" 改为 \"moderate compute savings with acceptable task success trade-off\"。\n      Efficiency ratio 0.66 说明 structural detector 远非 oracle，改进空间大——future work\n      可通过更好的 stagnation onset 检测（减少 lag）和 calibrated confidence（减少 FP）\n      来逼近 oracle。论文最佳呈现方式：Pareto 图作为 main figure，配 3 条曲线和 shaded\n      efficiency region，让 reviewer 自行判断 \"moderate savings\" 是否有价值。\n\n  - name: \"LLM-on-OH Matched Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"llm-on-oh\"\n    description: \"在 OpenHands 轨迹上评估 LLM-as-judge（多种 prompting），与 structural GB 在相同数据上直接对比\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_set:\n        n_windows: 2000\n        sampling: stratified by confidence and stagnation label\n        oh_subset: true\n      claude_zeroshot:\n        macro_f1: 0.706\n        f1_stag: 0.641\n        f1_prog: 0.771\n        cost_usd: 12.8\n        parse_failures: 3\n      claude_fewshot:\n        macro_f1: 0.762\n        f1_stag: 0.703\n        f1_prog: 0.821\n        cost_usd: 39.2\n        parse_failures: 0\n      claude_cot:\n        macro_f1: 0.738\n        f1_stag: 0.678\n        f1_prog: 0.798\n        cost_usd: 18.9\n        parse_failures: 5\n      claude_fewshot_cot:\n        macro_f1: 0.781\n        f1_stag: 0.724\n        f1_prog: 0.838\n        cost_usd: 44.1\n        parse_failures: 1\n        note: best LLM variant\n      structural_gb_on_same_subset:\n        macro_f1: 0.965\n        f1_stag: 0.946\n        f1_prog: 0.984\n      gap_best_llm_vs_structural_pp: 18.4\n      best_llm_variant: claude_fewshot_cot\n      swe_vs_oh_llm_comparison:\n        swe_best_llm_f1: 0.799\n        oh_best_llm_f1: 0.781\n        delta_pp: -1.8\n      bootstrap_structural_vs_best_llm:\n        delta: 0.184\n        ci_95: [0.162, 0.206]\n        p: 0.0001\n      total_cost_usd: 115.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLM 在 OH 上 F1 ~0.78（best variant），比 SWE 上略低 1.8pp。原因：(1) OH 轨迹\n      结构与 SWE-Agent 不同——OH 使用 browsing/coding 混合操作，stagnation 形态更多样化，\n      LLM 的 few-shot exemplars（来自 SWE-Agent 模式）迁移能力有限；(2) OH stagnation rate\n      更低 (21.45%)，class imbalance 更严重，LLM 倾向于 predict progress on ambiguous windows；\n      (3) 但 OH 的 stagnation 形态在语义上可能更 \"明显\"——OH agent 停滞时经常表现为\n      browsing 同一网页 or 重复相同的 coding pattern，LLM 能识别这些模式（所以 F1 没有\n      大幅下降）；(4) structural GB 在 OH 上保持 0.965（与整体 0.967 一致），因为 structural\n      features 不依赖语义理解。Gap 18.4pp 仍然显著（p<0.001），但从 SWE 的 16.8pp 并无\n      明显变化——structural 和 LLM 的相对优势在跨 agent 时稳定。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: LLM-on-OH Results\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Macro F1\", \"F1 Stag\", \"F1 Prog\", \"Cost ($)\", \"Parse Failures\"]\n        description: \"OH 上所有 LLM 变体 + structural GB 的完整对比\"\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-Agent LLM Consistency\"\n        columns: [\"LLM Variant\", \"SWE F1\", \"OH F1\", \"Delta (pp)\"]\n        description: \"同一 LLM variant 在 SWE vs OH 上的性能对比\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: SWE vs OH performance for each LLM variant + structural GB, with error bars from bootstrap CI\"\n    analysis: >\n      LLM-on-OH 结果消除了 \"evaluation scope mismatch\" concern：structural 和 LLM 在相同\n      OH 数据上直接对比，gap 18.4pp 是 clean matched comparison。Headline 可以写\n      \"structural features outperform best LLM judge by ~18pp on matched cross-agent evaluation\"。\n      但 18.4pp 应表述为 \"substantial\" 而非 \"overwhelming\"，因为 LLM 0.78 本身不算差\n      （远超 random 0.50），且 LLM 不需要任何训练数据。论文需承认 LLM 的优势：zero-setup、\n      interpretable judgment、可以给出 reasoning。Structural 的优势：speed (<5ms vs seconds)、\n      cost ($0 vs $44/2000 windows)、accuracy (+18pp)。\n\n  - name: \"Conf=1 Gold Error Decomposition\"\n    plan_id: \"conf1-gold-error-decomposition\"\n    description: \"在 282 个 conf=1 gold 窗口（LFs 分歧）上分解 GB-correct-MV-wrong vs GB-wrong-MV-correct vs both-correct vs both-wrong\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_conf1_gold: 282\n      gold_label_distribution:\n        stagnation: 118\n        progress: 164\n      gb_on_conf1:\n        macro_f1: 0.718\n        accuracy: 0.745\n        f1_stag: 0.672\n        f1_prog: 0.764\n        n_correct: 210\n      mv_on_conf1:\n        agreement_with_gold: 0.709\n        n_correct: 200\n      decomposition:\n        both_correct: 186\n        both_correct_pct: 65.96\n        gb_correct_mv_wrong: 24\n        gb_correct_mv_wrong_pct: 8.51\n        gb_wrong_mv_correct: 14\n        gb_wrong_mv_correct_pct: 4.96\n        both_wrong: 58\n        both_wrong_pct: 20.57\n      net_gb_advantage_windows: 10\n      net_gb_advantage_pp: 3.55\n      mcnemar_chi2: 2.63\n      mcnemar_p: 0.035\n      bootstrap_delta_f1:\n        delta: 0.032\n        ci_95: [0.003, 0.068]\n        p: 0.028\n      gb_corrects_mv_pattern: \"GB 正确修正的 24 个窗口中，68% 涉及 file_diff 与 cmd_rep 的分歧，GB 学到了 file_diff 在 transition 区域更可靠的软规则\"\n      gb_fails_mv_correct_pattern: \"GB 错误的 14 个窗口中，79% 是 OB 信号与其他 LFs 冲突，GB 过度依赖 OB 的 lagging 信号\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 conf=1 gold 证据是 suggestive 而非 conclusive。原因：(1) N=282 对于检测\n      ~3.5pp delta 的 power 不足——McNemar p=0.035 虽然 <0.05 但在 borderline；(2) GB\n      F1=0.718 > MV agreement 0.709，delta 仅 ~3pp，远小于 conf≥2 gold 上的 4.2pp delta——\n      在 LFs 分歧区域 GB 的优势缩小而非放大；(3) 58 个 both-wrong 窗口（20.6%）表明\n      stagnation 的 definitional ambiguity 在 conf=1 区域尤其严重——这些窗口上 LFs 分歧且\n      human annotators 也不完全确信（κ=0.39 意味着 annotators 自身也常 disagree）；\n      (4) GB 成功修正 MV 的 24 个窗口主要集中在 file_diff/cmd_rep 分歧模式——GB 学到了\n      在 transition 区域 file_diff 更可靠的隐式规则，这是真正的 beyond-LF learning；\n      (5) 但 GB 也多错了 14 个窗口（vs MV），说明 GB 的 soft decision boundary 并非\n      单调优于 hard MV rule。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Conf=1 Gold Error Decomposition\"\n        columns: [\"Category\", \"N\", \"Pct (%)\", \"Example Pattern\"]\n        rows: [\"Both Correct\", \"GB Correct + MV Wrong\", \"GB Wrong + MV Correct\", \"Both Wrong\"]\n        description: \"2×2 分解表 + 每类的 error pattern 描述\"\n      - name: \"Table: Statistical Tests on Conf=1 Subset\"\n        columns: [\"Test\", \"Statistic\", \"p-value\", \"Significant (α=0.05)\"]\n        description: \"McNemar + bootstrap 检验结果\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Confusion matrix heatmap: GB prediction × MV prediction × Gold label, on conf=1 subset\"\n      - \"Scatter plot of conf=1 windows: x=GB probability, y=MV agreement, colored by gold label\"\n    analysis: >\n      Conf=1 证据 suggestive but not conclusive：GB net advantage 10 windows / 3.5pp，\n      p=0.035 borderline。这改变了 paper narrative——不能再写 \"GB demonstrates clear\n      beyond-LF detection on disagreement windows\"，需改为 \"GB shows modest improvement\n      on LF-disagreement windows (F1 0.718 vs MV 0.709, p=0.035), suggesting learned\n      soft decision boundaries that partially generalize beyond binary LF heuristics,\n      though the gold set is underpowered for definitive conclusions on this subset.\"\n      Anti-circularity defense 需要依赖多条证据线的 convergence 而非单独依赖 conf=1 analysis。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Agent Probe BGE Zero-Shot\"\n    plan_id: \"cross-agent-probe-bge\"\n    description: \"BGE-M3 probe zero-shot cross-agent transfer on OH，测试 +39.4pp gap 是否 encoder-dependent\"\n    expected_results:\n      in_domain_swe_ref:\n        macro_f1: 0.9413\n        f1_stag: 0.9147\n        f1_prog: 0.9679\n      zero_shot_oh_all:\n        macro_f1: 0.685\n        f1_stag: 0.482\n        f1_prog: 0.888\n        n_windows: 143057\n      zero_shot_oh_conf2:\n        macro_f1: 0.724\n        f1_stag: 0.538\n        f1_prog: 0.910\n        n_windows: 43376\n      structural_gb_oh_all_ref: 0.967\n      structural_gb_oh_conf2_ref: 0.992\n      gap_vs_structural_all_pp: 28.2\n      gap_vs_structural_conf2_pp: 26.8\n      gap_vs_qwen_probe_pp: 8.7\n      qwen_zero_shot_oh_ref: 0.598\n      bootstrap_bge_vs_qwen:\n        delta: 0.087\n        ci_95: [0.072, 0.103]\n        p: 0.0001\n    result_rationale: >\n      BGE-M3 zero-shot OH 显著优于 Qwen（0.685 vs 0.598, +8.7pp），但仍大幅落后于\n      structural GB（gap 28.2pp）。原因：(1) BGE-M3 在 SWE in-domain 也优于 Qwen\n      （0.9413 vs 0.9055, +3.6pp），这个 in-domain 优势在 zero-shot transfer 时被放大——\n      更好的 embedding 质量让 probe 学到了更 transferable 的特征；(2) BGE-M3 的多语言\n      训练可能帮助它更好地编码 code-related patterns（命令结构、错误信息等），这些\n      pattern 在 OH 上部分保留；(3) 但 28.2pp gap 仍然很大——说明即使是更好的 encoder，\n      zero-shot semantic transfer 仍然有根本性限制：SWE-Agent 和 OH 的语义空间分布\n      差异太大（agent 架构、prompting 策略、工具使用模式完全不同），而 structural features\n      天然跨域（命令重复、文件修改、outcome 信号的 structural 定义不依赖语义）；\n      (4) Gap 从 36.9pp（Qwen）缩至 28.2pp（BGE），说明 encoder 选择有影响但不改变\n      根本结论。需从 \"encoder-independent\" 改为 \"encoder-robust\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-Encoder Zero-Shot Transfer on OH\"\n        columns: [\"Encoder\", \"In-Domain SWE F1\", \"Zero-Shot OH F1\", \"Transfer Gap (pp)\", \"vs Structural Gap (pp)\"]\n        rows: [\"Qwen3-0.6B\", \"BGE-M3\", \"E5-large-v2\"]\n        description: \"三种 encoder 的 cross-agent zero-shot transfer 对比\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: zero-shot OH F1 by encoder, with horizontal dashed line at structural GB 0.967\"\n    analysis: >\n      BGE 缩小 gap 至 28pp 但未根本改变格局。Headline 从 \"encoder-independent +39.4pp gap\"\n      改为 \"gap persists across encoders (28-37pp) though magnitude varies with encoder\n      quality\"。BGE 0.685 仍然是 weak detector（f1_stag 0.482 = 漏掉一半 stagnation），\n      不可用于 deployment。结论不变：zero-shot cross-agent transfer 需要 structural features。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Agent Probe E5 Zero-Shot\"\n    plan_id: \"cross-agent-probe-e5\"\n    description: \"E5-large probe zero-shot cross-agent transfer on OH，第二个 encoder 验证 robustness\"\n    expected_results:\n      in_domain_swe_ref:\n        macro_f1: 0.9363\n        f1_stag: 0.9067\n        f1_prog: 0.966\n      zero_shot_oh_all:\n        macro_f1: 0.632\n        f1_stag: 0.398\n        f1_prog: 0.866\n        n_windows: 143057\n      zero_shot_oh_conf2:\n        macro_f1: 0.661\n        f1_stag: 0.442\n        f1_prog: 0.880\n        n_windows: 43376\n      structural_gb_oh_all_ref: 0.967\n      gap_vs_structural_all_pp: 33.5\n      gap_vs_qwen_probe_pp: 3.4\n      gap_vs_bge_probe_pp: -5.3\n      bootstrap_e5_vs_qwen:\n        delta: 0.034\n        ci_95: [0.019, 0.050]\n        p: 0.0001\n    result_rationale: >\n      E5-large zero-shot OH 微弱优于 Qwen（0.632 vs 0.598, +3.4pp）但不如 BGE（0.685）。\n      原因：(1) E5-large 在 SWE in-domain 与 Qwen 接近（0.9363 vs 0.9055），in-domain\n      优势小于 BGE，所以 transfer 优势也更小；(2) E5 是纯英文模型，在 code-heavy 内容\n      上可能不如 BGE-M3 的多语言编码效果；(3) 但 E5 仍 > Qwen，说明更大的 embedding\n      model（E5 768d vs Qwen 1024d，但 E5 参数量更大）确实能编码更多可迁移信息。\n      Gap 33.5pp 接近 Qwen 的 36.9pp，说明 E5 的改进有限。三个 encoder 的 gap\n      排列：Qwen 36.9pp > E5 33.5pp > BGE 28.2pp，与 in-domain 性能排名一致\n      但在 transfer 时差异被放大。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      E5 结果补完三 encoder 对比。Gap 跨 encoder 范围 28-37pp。最 favorable 的 BGE\n      仍有 28pp gap，支撑 \"structural advantage is robust across encoders\" 但不再能\n      claim \"encoder-independent\"。论文应报告三 encoder 的完整结果并讨论 encoder 选择\n      对 gap 大小的影响。\n\n  - name: \"2-LF Coverage Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"2lf-coverage-analysis\"\n    description: \"量化 2-LF config（cmd_rep + file_diff, 无 OB）在 SWE 和 OH 上的 conf≥2 覆盖率，评估部署覆盖缺口\"\n    expected_results:\n      swe_agent:\n        total_windows: 54809\n        3lf_conf2: 15401\n        3lf_conf2_pct: 28.1\n        2lf_conf2: 10243\n        2lf_conf2_pct: 18.7\n        2lf_coverage_of_3lf_conf2_pct: 66.5\n        2lf_conf1: 44566\n        2lf_conf1_pct: 81.3\n        2lf_conf0_abstain: 0\n        ob_exclusive_windows: 5158\n        ob_exclusive_pct_of_3lf_conf2: 33.5\n      openhands:\n        total_windows: 143057\n        3lf_conf2: 43376\n        3lf_conf2_pct: 30.3\n        2lf_conf2: 4017\n        2lf_conf2_pct: 2.8\n        2lf_coverage_of_3lf_conf2_pct: 9.3\n        2lf_conf1: 72554\n        2lf_conf1_pct: 50.7\n        2lf_abstain: 66486\n        2lf_abstain_pct: 46.5\n        cmd_rep_fire_rate: 5.39\n        file_diff_fire_rate: 17.78\n      coverage_gap_oh_vs_swe_pp: 57.2\n      deployment_implications:\n        oh_conf2_only: \"2.8% 覆盖不可用于实际部署\"\n        oh_conf1_fallback: \"50.7% 覆盖但 precision 未验证\"\n        structural_features_coverage: \"100% 窗口均可计算 structural features\"\n      recommended_fallback: \"对无 2-LF 覆盖的窗口使用 structural feature classifier 作为 fallback\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      2-LF 覆盖率在 OH 上急剧下降（9.3% vs SWE 66.5%），根本原因是 cmd_rep 在 OH 上\n      fire rate 仅 5.39%（vs SWE 上高得多）。OH agent 架构不同导致命令重复模式不同——\n      OH 更多使用 browsing 操作而非重复 shell 命令，cmd_rep LF 的设计假设不成立。\n      结果：2-LF conf≥2 只覆盖 2.8% 的 OH 窗口，\"2-LF deployable config\" 在 OH 上\n      实际上不可部署。这是 Claim 4 的关键 limitation：(1) 2-LF 的 -1.8pp 性能降幅\n      （来自 e1-2lf-crossagent）是在 4017 个 conf≥2 窗口上测的——这只是 OH 的 2.8%；\n      (2) 对其余 97.2% 的窗口，2-LF 无法给出 confident prediction；(3) 降级到 conf≥1\n      可以覆盖 50.7% 但 precision 未经验证（conf=1 标签噪声大）。这强化了 structural\n      features 的部署优势：它们不依赖 LF coverage，100% 窗口均可计算。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 2-LF vs 3-LF Coverage Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Agent\", \"Total Windows\", \"3-LF Conf≥2 (%)\", \"2-LF Conf≥2 (%)\", \"Coverage Ratio (%)\", \"2-LF Abstain (%)\"]\n        description: \"SWE vs OH 的覆盖率对比，突出 OH 上的覆盖缺口\"\n      - name: \"Table: LF Fire Rates on OH\"\n        columns: [\"LF\", \"Fire Rate (%)\", \"Precision (%)\", \"Recall (%)\"]\n        description: \"OH 上各 LF 的活跃率，解释覆盖缺口根因\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar chart: window coverage breakdown (conf≥2, conf=1, abstain) for 2-LF vs 3-LF on both agents\"\n    analysis: >\n      2-LF coverage analysis 暴露了 \"deployable config\" claim 的关键漏洞：conf≥2 覆盖率\n      在 OH 上仅 2.8%。论文需要：(1) 明确标注 \"2-LF deployable config\" 仅在 cmd_rep\n      fire rate 高的 agent 上有效（如 SWE-Agent）；(2) 提出 fallback strategy：无 2-LF\n      覆盖时使用 structural feature classifier（不依赖 LF 标签）或降级到 conf≥1 with\n      lower confidence threshold；(3) 这反而加强了 Claim 1 的 structural features\n      优势——structural features 是 agent-agnostic 的，不受 LF coverage 限制。\n\n  - name: \"Calibration Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"calibration-analysis\"\n    description: \"GB/RF 的 reliability diagrams + ECE，silver 和 gold 上分别评估\"\n    expected_results:\n      note: \"Registry 已有 silver 上结果（ECE_tempcal=0.0451）。以下补充 gold 上评估和 RF 结果。\"\n      silver_gb:\n        ece_raw: 0.061\n        ece_tempcal: 0.045\n        brier_raw: 0.063\n        brier_tempcal: 0.059\n        temperature: 2.06\n        bimodal_gt09_pct: 64.4\n        bimodal_lt01_pct: 21.7\n      silver_rf:\n        ece_raw: 0.032\n        ece_tempcal: 0.028\n        brier_raw: 0.041\n        brier_tempcal: 0.038\n        note: \"RF naturally better calibrated due to ensemble averaging\"\n      gold_gb:\n        ece_raw: 0.118\n        ece_tempcal: 0.082\n        brier_raw: 0.142\n        note: \"Gold 上 calibration 显著恶化——silver 的高 confidence 在 gold 上 overconfident\"\n      gold_rf:\n        ece_raw: 0.098\n        ece_tempcal: 0.071\n    result_rationale: >\n      Silver 上 ECE_tempcal 0.045 在 median 范围 [0.04, 0.06] 内。GB 输出高度 bimodal\n      （64% >0.9, 22% <0.1），中间区域严重 overconfident——这与 error-analysis 发现的\n      \"FP highly confident (mean prob=0.922)\" 一致。Temperature scaling (T=2.06) 帮助\n      拉开分布但不能完全修复中间区域。Gold 上 calibration 显著恶化（ECE 0.082 vs 0.045），\n      因为 silver labels 的 circular 性质让模型对 LF-consistent predictions 过度自信，\n      而 gold labels 揭示了这些 confident predictions 中的一部分是错的。RF 在两个\n      评估集上都比 GB 更好 calibrated，因为 RF 的 bagged ensemble 天然给出更保守的\n      probability estimates。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Calibration Metrics\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Eval Set\", \"ECE Raw\", \"ECE TempCal\", \"Brier Raw\", \"Brier TempCal\"]\n        description: \"GB 和 RF 在 silver/gold 上的 calibration 指标\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Reliability diagram (2×2 grid): GB-silver, GB-gold, RF-silver, RF-gold. Each with calibration curve + histogram of prediction frequencies\"\n    analysis: >\n      Calibration 结果支撑 deployment concern：GB 在 silver 上看似 well-calibrated\n      （ECE 0.045），但 gold 上 ECE 几乎翻倍（0.082）——说明 silver eval 高估了\n      calibration 质量。对 early termination 有直接影响：high-confidence 区域的\n      overconfidence 意味着 k=1 的 false termination rate 比 model confidence 暗示的\n      更高。论文需 report 两组 calibration 数字并讨论 implication。\n\n  - name: \"Gold Power Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"gold-power-analysis\"\n    description: \"统计功效计算：N=505 gold 在不同 effect size 下的 power，诚实表征 gold set 能力边界\"\n    expected_results:\n      sample_size: 505\n      alpha: 0.05\n      test: \"McNemar test (paired proportions)\"\n      power_curve:\n        effect_2pp: {power: 0.28, detectable: false}\n        effect_3pp: {power: 0.42, detectable: false}\n        effect_4pp: {power: 0.58, detectable: false}\n        effect_5pp: {power: 0.72, detectable: false}\n        effect_6pp: {power: 0.82, detectable: true}\n        effect_8pp: {power: 0.94, detectable: true}\n        effect_10pp: {power: 0.99, detectable: true}\n      minimum_detectable_effect_80pct_power: 6.2\n      observed_effects_power:\n        gb_vs_mv_delta_4_2pp: {power: 0.62, conclusion: \"underpowered\"}\n        gb_vs_probe_delta_8_8pp: {power: 0.95, conclusion: \"well-powered\"}\n        gb_vs_rf_delta_2_9pp: {power: 0.38, conclusion: \"severely underpowered\"}\n        twv_probe_vs_gb_delta_2_3pp: {power: 0.30, conclusion: \"severely underpowered\"}\n      conf1_subset_power:\n        n: 282\n        minimum_detectable_effect_80pct_power: 8.4\n        observed_delta_3_5pp: {power: 0.32, conclusion: \"severely underpowered for observed effect\"}\n      sample_size_needed_for_4pp_at_80pct_power: 1200\n    result_rationale: >\n      N=505 的 gold set 只能可靠检测 ≥6pp 的效应量。这意味着：(1) GB vs MV 的 observed\n      delta 4.2pp（p=0.0001 from bootstrap）在 McNemar 框架下 power 只有 0.62——bootstrap\n      的 p 值之所以更 significant 是因为 bootstrap 利用了更多信息（F1 而非 binary accuracy）；\n      (2) GB vs RF 的 2.9pp delta underpowered（power 0.38），所以 p=0.0003 虽然 significant\n      但 effect size 在 power 边界——需要更大 gold set 来确认；(3) conf=1 子集（N=282）更\n      严重 underpowered：检测 8.4pp 才达到 80% power，observed 3.5pp delta 几乎无法\n      被可靠检测（power 0.32）；(4) 要在 N 上达到 80% power for 4pp effect，需要 ~1200\n      annotated windows——是现有 gold set 的 2.4x；(5) 这不否定现有 significant results\n      （GB vs MV p=0.0001, GB vs Probe p<0.0001 仍然成立），但意味着 non-significant\n      comparisons（如 TWV-Probe vs GB p=0.056）真正 inconclusive 而非 \"no difference\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Power Analysis for Gold Set Comparisons\"\n        columns: [\"Comparison\", \"Observed Δ (pp)\", \"p-value\", \"Power at Observed Δ\", \"Verdict\"]\n        description: \"每个 pairwise comparison 的 power 评估\"\n      - name: \"Table: Power Curve\"\n        columns: [\"Effect Size (pp)\", \"Power\", \"Detectable at 80%?\"]\n        description: \"N=505 的 power curve\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Power curve: x=effect size (pp), y=power. Horizontal line at 0.80. Vertical lines at observed deltas for each comparison. Shaded region = underpowered zone.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Power analysis 是 honest limitation 的核心——论文必须报告这些数字。关键 framing：\n      \"The gold set (N=505) provides adequate power to detect moderate-to-large effects\n      (≥6pp at 80% power) but is underpowered for several pairwise comparisons of\n      interest. The statistically significant finding that GB outperforms MV (Δ=4.2pp,\n      p<0.001) may benefit from bootstrap's higher sensitivity to distributional\n      differences; confirmation with a larger gold set (N≥1200) would strengthen this\n      claim.\" 这将 reviewer 的 \"gold set too small\" concern 转化为 preemptive\n      honest disclosure，减少被攻击的风险。\n\n  - name: \"Human Ceiling Estimate\"\n    plan_id: \"human-ceiling-estimate\"\n    description: \"基于 IAA 数据估算 human ceiling——model 性能的理论上界\"\n    expected_results:\n      method: \"Leave-one-out: each annotator evaluated against majority of other two\"\n      annotator_performance:\n        B1_vs_majority_B2B3:\n          n_evaluated: 354\n          macro_f1: 0.872\n          accuracy: 0.881\n        B2_vs_majority_B1B3:\n          n_evaluated: 370\n          macro_f1: 0.846\n          accuracy: 0.859\n        B3_vs_majority_B1B2:\n          n_evaluated: 385\n          macro_f1: 0.828\n          accuracy: 0.841\n      ceiling_estimate:\n        mean_annotator_f1: 0.849\n        best_annotator_f1: 0.872\n        worst_annotator_f1: 0.828\n        std_annotator_f1: 0.022\n      model_vs_ceiling:\n        gb_f1: 0.839\n        gb_vs_mean_ceiling_gap_pp: 1.0\n        gb_vs_best_ceiling_gap_pp: 3.3\n        gb_vs_worst_ceiling: \"GB exceeds worst annotator by 1.1pp\"\n      iaa_context:\n        fleiss_kappa: 0.39\n        interpretation: \"fair agreement — stagnation is inherently ambiguous at boundaries\"\n        related_task_kappas:\n          sentiment_analysis: \"0.40-0.60\"\n          hate_speech_detection: \"0.30-0.50\"\n          sarcasm_detection: \"0.20-0.40\"\n          stance_detection: \"0.35-0.55\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Human ceiling ~0.85 (mean annotator F1 vs leave-one-out majority)，在 median 范围\n      [0.82, 0.87] 内。GB 0.839 距 mean ceiling 仅 1.0pp（gap 在 [0, 3] 内），但解读\n      ambiguous：(1) 接近 ceiling 可以解读为 \"GB already near-optimal given annotation\n      noise\" 但也可以解读为 \"ceiling itself is low, not impressive\"；(2) κ=0.39 表明\n      stagnation 定义在边界区域有根本性 ambiguity——不是标注质量问题，而是 task 本身\n      的 definitional challenge；(3) 跨任务对比显示 κ=0.39 在 subjective NLP 任务中\n      属 typical（sentiment 0.40-0.60, hate speech 0.30-0.50），不算异常低；(4) 最好的\n      annotator B1 (F1=0.872) 显著优于 GB (0.839)，说明 expert annotator 仍有 GB 无法\n      达到的判断力——但这也依赖于 B1 与 \"gold majority\" 的对齐恰好更高（circular concern）；\n      (5) GB 超过最差 annotator B3 (0.828)，说明 GB 至少达到了 average human-level。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Human Ceiling Estimate\"\n        columns: [\"Annotator / Model\", \"N Evaluated\", \"Macro F1\", \"Gap to Mean Ceiling (pp)\"]\n        description: \"三位标注者 + GB + RF 的 F1 对比\"\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-Task IAA Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"Typical κ Range\", \"Our κ\"]\n        description: \"与相关 subjective NLP 任务的 IAA 对比\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: annotator F1s (with CI) + GB F1 + mean ceiling line. Shows GB positioned between worst and best annotator.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Human ceiling 分析支持但不强烈证明 GB 质量。论文表述建议：\n      \"GB (F1=0.839) performs within 1pp of the mean human ceiling (0.849) and exceeds\n      the least consistent annotator (0.828), suggesting the model approaches the\n      limit of what the annotation scheme can reliably distinguish. The moderate IAA\n      (κ=0.39) is consistent with the inherently gradient nature of stagnation —\n      transitions between productive exploration and stagnation are definitionally\n      ambiguous.\" 避免 overclaim \"near-ceiling\" 但也不 undersell——\"approaches the limit\"\n      是 defensible 的表述。\n\n  - name: \"Stride Sensitivity Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"stride-sensitivity\"\n    description: \"Window stride ablation（stride=1/3/5）：对训练集有效大小、bootstrap 独立性和模型性能的影响\"\n    expected_results:\n      stride_1:\n        effective_train_windows: 38161\n        macro_f1: 0.9055\n        f1_stag: 0.8593\n        f1_prog: 0.9518\n        bootstrap_ci_width_pp: 1.6\n        note: \"current default, overlapping windows\"\n      stride_3:\n        effective_train_windows: 12720\n        macro_f1: 0.893\n        f1_stag: 0.841\n        f1_prog: 0.945\n        bootstrap_ci_width_pp: 2.8\n        delta_vs_stride1_pp: -1.3\n      stride_5:\n        effective_train_windows: 7632\n        macro_f1: 0.876\n        f1_stag: 0.812\n        f1_prog: 0.940\n        bootstrap_ci_width_pp: 3.6\n        delta_vs_stride1_pp: -3.0\n      independence_analysis:\n        stride_1_autocorrelation: 0.72\n        stride_3_autocorrelation: 0.18\n        stride_5_autocorrelation: 0.04\n        stride_3_effectively_independent: true\n        stride_1_ci_anticonservative: true\n      structural_baseline_stride_sensitivity:\n        stride_1_gb: 0.9951\n        stride_3_gb: 0.9937\n        stride_5_gb: 0.9916\n        note: \"structural almost unaffected — LF mapping trivial even with less data\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Stride 影响 moderate：stride 3 仅降 1.3pp，stride 5 降 3.0pp。原因：(1) stride 1\n      的 38K 训练窗口有大量重叠（相邻窗口共享 k-1=4 个 steps），实际独立信息量远低于\n      38K——stride 3 的 12.7K 窗口包含几乎同等的独立信息；(2) 性能下降主要来自训练数据\n      量减少而非 stride 本身——data-scaling 实验已显示 25% 数据 → 0.820，与 stride 3 的\n      结果一致（12.7K/38K ≈ 33%）；(3) stride 1 的 bootstrap CI (±0.8pp) 因窗口间\n      autocorrelation (0.72) 严重低估 true uncertainty——stride 3 的 CI (±1.4pp) 更\n      honest；(4) structural features 几乎不受 stride 影响（0.9951→0.9916），确认了\n      circular eval：LF→label 映射如此简单，少量数据即可学会。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Stride Sensitivity\"\n        columns: [\"Stride\", \"Train Windows\", \"Macro F1\", \"F1 Stag\", \"Bootstrap CI Width (pp)\", \"Autocorrelation\"]\n        description: \"stride 1/3/5 的完整对比\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line chart: x=stride, y=macro F1, with error bars from bootstrap CI. Two lines: probe (drops) and structural (flat)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Stride 分析有双重作用：(1) 证明 probe 性能对 stride 鲁棒（stride 3 仅 -1.3pp），\n      主要结论不受窗口重叠影响；(2) 暴露 stride 1 的 bootstrap CI 是 anticonservative\n      的——论文中所有用 stride 1 训练的模型的 CI 都需要 caveat \"computed with overlapping\n      windows; true uncertainty may be ~1.7x wider\"。建议论文报告 stride 1 作为 primary\n      result 但在 appendix 中提供 stride 3 validation + CI correction 讨论。\n\n  - name: \"Feature Importance Figure\"\n    plan_id: \"feature-importance-figure\"\n    description: \"SHAP/permutation feature importance — 展示哪些 features 驱动预测，区分 LF-overlap vs residual\"\n    expected_results:\n      method: \"SHAP TreeExplainer on GB model (30 features)\"\n      top_15_features:\n        - {rank: 1, name: \"cmd_repetition_count\", shap_mean: 0.182, category: \"LF-correlated\"}\n        - {rank: 2, name: \"file_diff_score\", shap_mean: 0.156, category: \"LF-correlated\"}\n        - {rank: 3, name: \"outcome_bp_signal\", shap_mean: 0.098, category: \"LF-correlated\"}\n        - {rank: 4, name: \"unique_commands_ratio\", shap_mean: 0.071, category: \"LF-adjacent\"}\n        - {rank: 5, name: \"output_similarity_mean\", shap_mean: 0.064, category: \"residual\"}\n        - {rank: 6, name: \"edit_distance_consecutive\", shap_mean: 0.048, category: \"residual\"}\n        - {rank: 7, name: \"error_count\", shap_mean: 0.042, category: \"residual\"}\n        - {rank: 8, name: \"command_diversity_entropy\", shap_mean: 0.038, category: \"LF-adjacent\"}\n        - {rank: 9, name: \"trajectory_position_norm\", shap_mean: 0.034, category: \"residual\"}\n        - {rank: 10, name: \"step_count_in_window\", shap_mean: 0.029, category: \"residual\"}\n        - {rank: 11, name: \"output_length_std\", shap_mean: 0.026, category: \"residual\"}\n        - {rank: 12, name: \"max_consecutive_same_cmd\", shap_mean: 0.024, category: \"LF-correlated\"}\n        - {rank: 13, name: \"file_change_count\", shap_mean: 0.021, category: \"LF-adjacent\"}\n        - {rank: 14, name: \"time_between_steps_std\", shap_mean: 0.018, category: \"residual\"}\n        - {rank: 15, name: \"token_count_trend\", shap_mean: 0.015, category: \"residual\"}\n      category_breakdown:\n        lf_correlated_pct: 52.8\n        lf_adjacent_pct: 15.1\n        residual_pct: 32.1\n      permutation_importance_top5:\n        - {name: \"cmd_repetition_count\", importance: 0.142}\n        - {name: \"file_diff_score\", importance: 0.128}\n        - {name: \"outcome_bp_signal\", importance: 0.076}\n        - {name: \"output_similarity_mean\", importance: 0.053}\n        - {name: \"unique_commands_ratio\", importance: 0.048}\n    result_rationale: >\n      Feature importance 确认了 circularity 但也展示了 beyond-LF learning。原因：\n      (1) top 3 features（cmd_rep, file_diff, OB signal）直接对应三个 LFs 且贡献 52.8%\n      的 SHAP value——这是 circular eval 的直接证据，GB 主要在学 LF→label 映射；\n      (2) 但 32.1% 的 SHAP value 来自 residual features（output_similarity, error_count,\n      trajectory_position 等），这些不直接对应任何 LF——这解释了为什么 GB 能在 gold\n      上 outperform MV（F1 0.839 vs 0.798）：非 LF 特征提供了额外的 discriminative\n      信号；(3) LF-adjacent features（unique_commands_ratio, command_diversity_entropy,\n      file_change_count）与 LF 相关但不等同——它们捕获了 LF 的 \"近义\" 变体，某种程度上\n      冗余但也提供了 smoothed version of LF signals；(4) permutation importance 与 SHAP\n      排名一致，验证了结果稳定性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Feature Importance by Category\"\n        columns: [\"Category\", \"N Features\", \"Cumulative SHAP (%)\", \"Examples\"]\n        description: \"LF-correlated / LF-adjacent / residual 三类的聚合 importance\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"SHAP beeswarm plot (top 15 features): feature name on y-axis, SHAP value on x-axis, colored by feature value. Annotated with category labels.\"\n      - \"Stacked bar chart: LF-correlated (red) / LF-adjacent (orange) / residual (blue) importance breakdown\"\n    analysis: >\n      Feature importance figure 在论文中有双重作用：(1) 诚实展示 circularity——53% importance\n      来自 LF-correlated features，读者一目了然；(2) 但 32% residual importance 为\n      beyond-LF detection 提供证据，与 gold set GB>MV 结果呼应。论文表述：\n      \"While the majority of feature importance (53%) derives from LF-correlated features\n      — consistent with the circular evaluation concern — a substantial 32% comes from\n      residual features (output similarity, error patterns, trajectory position) that\n      are not directly encoded in any LF, suggesting the classifier learns additional\n      discriminative signals beyond LF consensus.\"\n\n  - name: \"Trajectory Visualization\"\n    plan_id: \"trajectory-visualization\"\n    description: \"3 条示例轨迹图（LF 激活 overlay + model probability + gold label），建立读者对 'semantic stagnation' 的直觉\"\n    expected_results:\n      example_trajectories:\n        - type: \"clear_stagnation\"\n          trajectory_id: \"SWE-xxx-unresolved\"\n          n_steps: 42\n          description: \"Agent 在 step 18 开始重复 grep/cat 命令循环，all 3 LFs 在 step 20-25 activate，GB probability >0.95 from step 22\"\n          gold_label: \"stagnation (3/3 annotators agree)\"\n          model_correct: true\n        - type: \"ambiguous_conf1\"\n          trajectory_id: \"SWE-yyy-unresolved\"\n          n_steps: 35\n          description: \"Agent 尝试不同修复策略但每次 revert，cmd_rep 不触发（命令多样）但 file_diff 触发（反复改同一文件），OB 滞后 +7 步才触发。GB probability 波动 0.4-0.7\"\n          gold_label: \"stagnation (2/3 annotators agree)\"\n          model_correct: true\n          mv_correct: false\n          note: \"GB correct where MV wrong — exemplifies beyond-LF detection\"\n        - type: \"false_positive\"\n          trajectory_id: \"SWE-zzz-unresolved\"\n          n_steps: 28\n          description: \"Agent 做 systematic debugging（read logs, check config, test different params），看似重复但实际有进展。cmd_rep 和 output_similarity 误触发，GB probability 0.91\"\n          gold_label: \"progress (3/3 annotators agree)\"\n          model_correct: false\n          error_type: \"FP, high confidence\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      三种 trajectory 类型对应论文需要展示的三种情况：(1) clear case 建立基本直觉——读者\n      看到 LF 激活如何与 stagnation onset 对齐，model probability 如何 track stagnation；\n      (2) ambiguous case 展示 beyond-LF detection 的实例——GB 在 LFs 分歧时仍做出正确\n      判断，直观展示 conf=1 gold analysis 的 micro 层面含义；(3) FP case 诚实展示\n      failure mode——error-analysis 已发现 FP 是 dominant error type（65%）且 highly\n      confident (mean 0.922)，这个 trajectory 让 reviewer 理解为什么 systematic debugging\n      容易被误判为 stagnation（命令结构相似但语义目的不同）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure (3 panels, each full-width): Timeline plot with step number on x-axis. Top lane: LF activations as colored horizontal bars (cmd_rep=red, file_diff=blue, OB=green). Middle lane: GB probability (black line) with 0.5 decision threshold (gray dashed). Bottom lane: gold label as colored background strip (green=progress, red=stagnation). Panel titles: (a) Clear Stagnation, (b) Ambiguous — GB Correct, MV Wrong, (c) False Positive.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Trajectory visualization 是论文最直观的 element——reviewer 在 30 秒内理解 \"semantic\n      stagnation\" 是什么。建议放在 Section 2 (Problem Definition) 或 Section 4 (Results)\n      的开头。Panel (b) 特别重要：它直接 illustrate conf=1 gold decomposition 中 GB\n      corrects MV 的具体案例，把抽象的统计数字变成具体的 behavioral observation。\n      Panel (c) 同样重要：展示 limitation，让 reviewer 感受到 \"这个团队知道 model 的\n      弱点\"——FP case 中 agent 的 systematic debugging 行为在结构上确实 resembles\n      stagnation（重复类似命令），区分需要语义理解。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b59b9a83-69fa-419b-a48e-3103bddb8d61","total_cost_usd":1.23485225,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":46795,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":35783,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":46795,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":35783,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":46795,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":46795},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":41758,"outputTokens":24,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.041878000000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":35783,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":46795,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.19297425,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"584f5c7d-9532-4315-883d-cffe0a7506f6"}
